\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Two Critical Doctrinal Points Preserved\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 (1) The Father remains the One God throughout the Son's return.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The 
\f0\b Ancient of Days
\f2\b0  (the Father) gives the Son the kingdom (Dan 7:14).\
- The 
\f0\b kingdom was prepared by the Father
\f2\b0  from the foundation of the world (Matt 25:34).\
- 
\f0\b Only the Father
\f2\b0  knows the day and hour (Matt 24:36; Mark 13:32; Acts 1:7).\
- The blessed are blessed 
\f0\b of the Father
\f2\b0  (Matt 25:34).\
- The Day of the LORD = the Day of the Lord Jesus, because the Son comes in the Father's Name with the Father's authority.\
- The consummation: 
\f0\b "one LORD, one Name"
\f2\b0  (Zech 14:9) \'97 the unified worship of the One God.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 (2) The Son acts always in the Father's Name and by the Father's authority.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - He receives the kingdom from the Ancient of Days.\
- He returns at the Father's appointed time (which the Father alone knows).\
- He executes judgment by the authority 
\f0\b given
\f2\b0  to Him (John 5:22, 27).\
- His coming fulfills 
\f1\i both
\f2\i0  OT prophecies of the LORD's coming 
\f1\i and
\f2\i0  the Son of Man's coming \'97 because He is the LORD's Sent One, bearing the LORD's Name (Ex 23:21).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What This Means for Our Study\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Son's coming return is not the return of a second God or rival Deity. It is the visible, glorious appearing of the Father's Beloved Son, His Anointed Christ, His exalted Man, His high Priest forever \'97 coming to:\
- Vindicate His persecuted people.\
- Judge His enemies.\
- Establish the Father's universal Kingdom.\
- Be glorified in His saints.\
- Hand all things over to the Father (1 Cor 15:24-28, which we will examine in (C)).\
The pattern is unbroken from Genesis to the second coming: 
\f0\b the Father is the Source, the Son is the Sent One, and all things move toward the glory of God the Father.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What Remains\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We have now completed (A) and (B). What remains:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (C) The Son's final relation to the Father in the consummation
\f2\b0  \'97 1 Cor 15:24-28 \'97 perhaps the single most theologically decisive passage in all the NT on the Father-Son order at the end of all things. The Son delivers the Kingdom to the Father; the Son Himself is subjected to the Father; 
\f0\b God is all in all.
\f2\b0  This passage requires the utmost careful examination.\

\f0\b (D) The Son's titles and self-identifications in the Apocalypse
\f2\b0  \'97 the I AM sayings of Revelation, the Lamb on the Throne, Alpha and Omega designations, and how the Apocalypse weaves all our threads into the final tapestry.\
Shall we now proceed to 
\f0\b (C)
\f2\b0  \'97 1 Cor 15:24-28 \'97 the consummation passage?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Consummation \'97 1 Corinthians 15:20-28; the Father-Son Order at the End; the Direction Set: (C)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 C.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We now arrive at what may be the 
\f0\b single most theologically decisive passage in all the NT
\f2\b0  for the Father-Son order at the end of all things.\
This passage settles many questions that other texts only suggest. Paul writes here with deliberate precision, and we must read with the same care. Per our maxims, we will:\
1. Read the passage carefully in its full context (1 Cor 15:20-28).\
2. Examine each clause and its grammar.\
3. Cross-reference all relevant OT and NT witnesses.\
4. Let the whole counsel speak, and not flinch from what Paul plainly says.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b 1 CORINTHIANS 15:20-28 \'97 THE CONSUMMATION
\f2\b0 \
Let us first establish the full passage and then walk through it carefully.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1 Corinthians 15:20-22 \'97 The First Fruits\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 But now is Christ risen from the dead, and was made the first fruits of them that slept. For since by man came death, by man came also the resurrection of the dead. For as in Adam all die, even so in Christ shall all be made alive.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u960 \u945 \u961 \u967 \u8052  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u954 \u949 \u954 \u959 \u953 \u956 \u951 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u969 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "firstfruits of those who have fallen asleep."
\f2\i0  The risen Christ is the 
\f0\b firstfruits
\f2\b0  \'97 the first installment, guaranteeing the full harvest to follow.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \u8125  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u959 \u965  \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u948 \u953 \u8125  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u959 \u965  \u7936 \u957 \u940 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "through a man death, and through a man the resurrection."
\f2\i0  Paul is emphatic: 
\f0\b Christ is the Man
\f2\b0  through whom the resurrection comes. This is consistent with everything we have established \'97 the Mediator is 
\f0\b the Man Christ Jesus
\f2\b0  (1 Tim 2:5), the Son of Man of Daniel 7, the exalted Man at the Father's right hand.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1 Corinthians 15:23 \'97 The Order\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 But every man in his own order: the first fruits is Christ, afterward, they that are of Christ, at his coming shall rise again.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u964 \u940 \u947 \u956 \u945 
\f2\b0  = 
\f1\i order, rank, division
\f2\i0  \'97 a military term for a unit in formation. There is a precise sequence:\
1. 
\f0\b First:
\f2\b0  Christ \'97 already raised.\
2. 
\f0\b Then:
\f2\b0  Those who are Christ's \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u8115  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i at His coming.
\f2\i0  This is the 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 
\f2\b0  we examined in Matthew 24 \'97 the second appearing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1 Corinthians 15:24-28 \'97 The Heart of the Passage\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Now we come to the decisive verses. Let me present them in full first, then walk through them clause by clause.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Then shall be the end, when he hath delivered up the kingdom to God, even the Father, when he hath put down all rule, and all authority and power. For he must reign till he hath put all his enemies under his feet. The last enemy that shall be destroyed, is death. For he hath put down all things under his feet. (And when he saith that all things are subdued to him, it is manifest that he is excepted, which did put down all things under him.) And when all things shall be subdued unto him, then shall the Son also himself be subject unto him, that did subdue all things under him, that God may be all in all.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 CLAUSE-BY-CLAUSE EXAMINATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Clause 1: \uc0\u949 \u7990 \u964 \u945  \u964 \u8056  \u964 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u962  \'97 
\f3\i "Then comes the end"
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u964 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  = 
\f1\i the end, the goal, the consummation.
\f2\i0  Not merely a cessation, but the 
\f0\b completion
\f2\b0  of God's purposes. There is a definite eschatological endpoint \'97 what Paul calls 
\f0\b "the end."
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Clause 2: \uc0\u8005 \u964 \u945 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u948 \u953 \u948 \u8183  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u943  \'97 
\f3\i "when He delivers up the Kingdom to God, even the Father"
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is 
\f0\b the most consequential statement.
\f2\b0  Let us examine it carefully.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u948 \u953 \u948 \u8183 
\f2\b0  \'97 present subjunctive \'97 
\f1\i "when He hands over, delivers up, surrenders."
\f2\i0  The same verb used of Jesus being 
\f1\i "delivered up"
\f2\i0  for our sins (Rom 4:25). Now the Son 
\f0\b delivers up
\f2\b0  the Kingdom \'97 He hands it over.\

\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8052 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Kingdom."
\f2\i0  The very Kingdom that was given to Him by the Father (Dan 7:14; Matt 28:18) is now handed back.\

\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u943 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to the God and Father."
\f2\i0  This is grammatically critical. 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u943 
\f2\b0  uses 
\f0\b one article
