\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u954  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7944 \u961 \u957 \u943 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "out of the throne of God and of the Lamb."
\f2\i0  In the eternal state, 
\f0\b the throne
\f2\b0  (singular!) is shared by 
\f0\b God and the Lamb.
\f2\b0  The Father is on the throne; the Lamb is at His right hand (Ps 110:1) \'97 but the throne is one, jointly held in the consummation.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u7985  \u948 \u959 \u8166 \u955 \u959 \u953  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u955 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u949 \u973 \u963 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "His servants shall serve Him"
\f2\i0  (singular pronouns). The servants serve 
\f0\b Him
\f2\b0  \'97 and the antecedent is the combined "God and the Lamb" of the previous clause. The redeemed render unified worship to God and the Lamb together, 
\f0\b as one
\f2\b0 , because the Lamb's reign is unto the Father's glory and the Father acts through His Son.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8004 \u968 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u961 \u972 \u963 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "they shall see His face."
\f2\i0  The face that no man has seen (John 1:18; Ex 33:20) shall be seen in the eternal state \'97 through the mediation of the Lamb who declares the Father (John 1:18). This is the 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 the goal \'97 of all redemption.\
