\f0\b The Nature and Essence of the Father as Eternal Spirit
\f2\b0  \'97 which beautifully resolves the "singular throne" question, since Spirit is not confined to a location and the Lamb's session "at the right hand" is in a Spirit-pervaded heavenly reality, not a spatial throne-room of the kind a created mind imagines.\
2. 
\f0\b The Lord Jesus' prayer that the elect should become the habitation of God in Christ \'97 being one in Him even as the Son is in the Father.
\f2\b0  This is John 17:20-23 and the indwelling theme that runs from "I in them and Thou in Me" through Paul's "Christ in you, the hope of glory."\
Both of these will reframe and complete our entire study. I will hold them carefully and proceed to 
