\cf0 # 
\f0\b (D) \'97 THE SON IN THE APOCALYPSE
\f2\b0 \
The Apocalypse is the 
\f0\b concluding prophecy
\f2\b0  in our study \'97 and it is the place where every thread we have traced from Genesis 3:15 onward is gathered, illuminated, and consummated. Per our maxims, we will:\
1. Let the text speak in its order, beginning with Revelation 1.\
2. Examine every major title and self-identification of the Son.\
3. Carefully distinguish the Son's titles from the Father's where the text distinguishes them \'97 and note where titles are shared.\
4. Be cautious where the text is genuinely ambiguous, and not force resolution.\
5. Cross-reference all relevant OT and earlier NT witnesses.\
Let us proceed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
