\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 1:1 \'97 THE CHAIN OF REVELATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 The Revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave unto him, to show unto his servants things which must shortly be done: which he sent, and showed by his Angel unto his servant John,\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The very first verse establishes the 
\f0\b chain of revelation
\f2\b0 :\
1. 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  (the God = the Father) \'97 
\f0\b gives
\f2\b0  the revelation\
2. 
\f0\b to \uc0\u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  (Jesus Christ)\
3. who 
\f0\b sends His angel
\f2\b0 \
4. 
\f0\b to His servant John
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Father is the Source.
\f2\b0  Even at the climax of all prophecy, the chain begins with the Father. The Apocalypse is not Jesus' independent vision \'97 it is 
\f0\b what the Father gave Him.
\f2\b0  This perfectly continues the pattern we established throughout: 
\f1\i "the Son can do nothing of Himself"
\f2\i0  (John 5:19); 
\f1\i "the Father showeth Him all things"
\f2\i0  (John 5:20); 
\f1\i "only the Father knows"
\f2\i0  (Mark 13:32).\
This single verse is the 
\f0\b interpretive key
\f2\b0  for the entire book. Whatever the Apocalypse reveals about the Son, it begins with the Son 
\f0\b receiving
\f2\b0  from the Father what He then communicates.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 1:4-5 \'97 THE TRIPARTITE GREETING\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 John, to the seven Churches which are in Asia, Grace be with you, and peace from him, Which is, and Which was, and Which is to come, and from the seven Spirits which are before his Throne, And from Jesus Christ, which is that faithful witness, and that first begotten of the dead, and that Prince of the Kings of the earth, \'85\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the One who is, and who was, and who is to come."
\f2\i0  This is the title of 
\f0\b the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 the One who has eternal being, who was, who is, who is to come. It is John's expansion of the 
\f0\b \uc0\u7960 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u8001  \u8036 \u957 
\f2\b0  ("I AM the One Who Is") of Exodus 3:14 LXX.\

\f0\b Note carefully:
\f2\b0  The phrase is grammatically anomalous \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u8001  \u8036 \u957 
\f2\b0  keeps the title in the nominative even after the preposition 
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u960 \u972 
\f2\b0 . This is John's deliberate signal that 
\f0\b this is a divine Name
\f2\b0  that cannot be inflected \'97 it stands fixed as 
\f0\b THE ONE WHO IS, WAS, AND IS COMING
\f2\b0 . This is the Father, the eternal LORD.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8182 \u957  \u7953 \u960 \u964 \u8048  \u960 \u957 \u949 \u965 \u956 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u7939  \u7952 \u957 \u974 \u960 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u965  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the seven Spirits which are before His throne."
\f2\i0  The seven Spirits \'97 sometimes understood as the fullness of the Spirit (Isa 11:2 LXX names seven aspects of the Spirit of the LORD); sometimes understood as seven distinct spirits or angels before the throne. 
\f0\b Honest assessment:
\f2\b0  the text does not unambiguously decide. We will not press it.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 explicitly named third in the greeting, with these titles:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u956 \u940 \u961 \u964 \u965 \u962  \u8001  \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the faithful witness"
\f2\i0  (cf. Ps 89:37 LXX; Isa 55:4)\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u960 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u972 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8182 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the firstborn of the dead"
\f2\i0  (cf. Col 1:18 \'97 fulfilling Ps 2:7 / Acts 13:33)\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u7940 \u961 \u967 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u941 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u947 \u8134 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the ruler of the kings of the earth"
\f2\i0  (fulfilling Ps 89:27 LXX and Dan 7:14)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The greeting carefully 
\f0\b distinguishes the Father (the One who is, was, and is to come) from Jesus Christ
\f2\b0 , with the seven Spirits between them. This is 
\f1\i not
\f2\i0  a "trinitarian" formula in the post-Nicene sense \'97 the seven Spirits are not identical to "the Holy Spirit" in any creedal way, and the structure is not "three persons of one substance." But it is a 
\f0\b threefold greeting
\f2\b0  that links the Father, the Spirit(s), and the Son in salutation \'97 preserving distinction throughout.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 1:5-6 \'97 THE DOXOLOGY TO CHRIST\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Unto him that loved us, and washed us from our sins in his blood, And made us Kings and Priests unto God even his Father, to him I say be glory, and dominion for evermore, Amen.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of supreme importance for our study\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u960 \u959 \u943 \u951 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957 , \u7985 \u949 \u961 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u8054  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He made us a Kingdom, priests 
\f3\b to the God and Father of Him
\f1\b0 ."
\f2\i0 \
Notice carefully: 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u8054  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to His God and Father."
\f2\i0  This is the same construction as 
\f0\b 1 Cor 15:24
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i "to the God and Father"
\f2\i0 ) \'97 using one article governing two designations. The God is the Father.\

\f0\b And He is "His God and Father"
\f2\b0  \'97 i.e., 
\f0\b the God of Jesus Christ.
\f2\b0  This continues the consistent pattern: Jesus has a God; that God is the Father (John 20:17; Eph 1:17). Even in the Apocalypse, with all its exalted Christology, 
\f0\b the Father is the God of Jesus Christ.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u7969  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to Him be glory and dominion."
\f2\i0  Doxology is rendered to Jesus. This is consistent with Phil 2:11 \'97 confession of Jesus as Lord, 
\f1\i to the glory of God the Father.
\f2\i0  The doxology to the Son flows to the Father's glory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 1:7 \'97 HE COMETH WITH CLOUDS\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Behold, he cometh with clouds, and every eye shall see him: yea, even they which pierced him through: and all kinreds 
\f1\i (kindreds)
\f2\i0  of the earth shall wail before him, Even so, Amen.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Already examined under (B). This verse weaves together 
\f0\b Daniel 7:13
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i "coming with clouds"
\f2\i0 ) and 
\f0\b Zechariah 12:10
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i "they shall look on Him whom they pierced"
\f2\i0 ) \'97 establishing at the very threshold of the Apocalypse that the Son of Man of Daniel and the pierced One of Zechariah are 
