\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 1:12-16 \'97 THE VISION OF THE SON OF MAN\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Then I turned back to see the voice, that spake with me: and when I was turned, I saw seven golden candlesticks, And in the midst of the seven candlesticks, one like unto the Son of man, clothed with a garment down to the feet, and girded about the paps with a golden girdle. His head, and hairs were white as white wool, and as snow, and his eyes were as a flame of fire, And his feet like unto fine brass, burning as in a furnace: and his voice as the sound of many waters. And he had in his right hand seven stars: and out of his mouth went a sharp two edged sword: and his face shone as the sun shineth in his strength.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of the highest importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8005 \u956 \u959 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u965 \u7985 \u8056 \u957  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "like a Son of Man."
\f2\i0  This is the 
\f0\b Daniel 7:13 figure
\f2\b0  \'97 and now we see Him directly. 
\f0\b Jesus retains His humanity in His exalted state
\f2\b0  \'97 He is 
\f1\i "like a son of man,"
\f2\i0  still bearing the form of the incarnate Christ.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7969  \u954 \u949 \u966 \u945 \u955 \u8052  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u945 \u7985  \u964 \u961 \u943 \u967 \u949 \u962  \u955 \u949 \u965 \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8033 \u962  \u7956 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u955 \u949 \u965 \u954 \u972 \u957 , \u8033 \u962  \u967 \u953 \u974 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "His head and hairs white as white wool, as snow."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b This is a striking detail.
\f2\b0  Compare 
\f0\b Daniel 7:9 LXX:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i \cf0 "...\uc0\u8001  \u952 \u961 \u8054 \u958  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u949 \u966 \u945 \u955 \u8134 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8033 \u963 \u949 \u8054  \u7956 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u945 \u961 \u972 \u957 ..."
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "the hair of His head as pure wool..."
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f0\b describing the Ancient of Days (the Father).
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Honest theological observation:
\f2\b0  The risen Christ in Revelation 1 bears the appearance of the Ancient of Days described in Daniel 7. He is described in features Daniel attributed to the Father.\

\f0\b How do we honestly handle this per our maxims?
\f2\b0 \
We must be careful. The text 
\f0\b does not say
\f2\b0  the Son IS the Ancient of Days \'97 Daniel 7 explicitly distinguishes them, and Jesus Himself cited Daniel 7 of His being 
\f1\i brought before
\f2\i0  the Ancient of Days, not as being Him. What the text 
\f0\b does
\f2\b0  show is that 
\f0\b the Son, in His glorified state, bears features of the Father's appearance
\f2\b0  \'97 because He is 
\f0\b the \uc0\u949 \u7984 \u954 \u8060 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u959 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  (Col 1:15), 
\f0\b the \uc0\u7936 \u960 \u945 \u973 \u947 \u945 \u963 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u951 \u962  and \u967 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u964 \u8052 \u961  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u8017 \u960 \u959 \u963 \u964 \u940 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  (Heb 1:3) \'97 the Image, the Radiance, the exact Impression of the Father.\
The Son's glorified appearance 
\f0\b reflects and bears
\f2\b0  the Father's glory. This is consistent with John 17:5 \'97 
\f1\i "glorify Me with the glory I had with You before the world was."
\f2\i0  The Son's glory is the Father's glory shared with Him.\
So we note honestly: 
\f0\b the Son in His glorified state shares the visible glory of the Father, without being identical to the Father.
\f2\b0  The Lamb is the 
\f0\b Image
\f2\b0  through whom the Father's glory is seen (Rev 21:23 \'97 
\f1\i "the glory of God did light it: and the Lamb is the light thereof"
\f2\i0 ).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 1:17-18 \'97 THE FIRST AND THE LAST, THE LIVING ONE\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead: then he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not: I am that first and that last, And am alive, but I was dead: and behold, I am alive for evermore, Amen: and I have the keys of hell and of death.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u8001  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7956 \u963 \u967 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I am the First and the Last."
\f2\i0  This is a direct echo of 
\f0\b Isaiah 44:6 LXX
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b 48:12 LXX
\f2\b0  \'97 which we examined at the foundation of our study:\

\f0\b Isaiah 44:6 LXX:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i \cf0 "...\uc0\u7960 \u947 \u8060  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u945 \u8166 \u964 \u945 , \u960 \u955 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 1599 Geneva:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "...I am the first, and I am the last, and without me is there no God."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Isaiah 48:12 LXX:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i \cf0 "...\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 ."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 1599 Geneva:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "...I am, I am the first, and I am the last."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Honest theological assessment:
\f2\b0  In Isaiah, 
\f0\b "the First and the Last"
\f2\b0  is the LORD's own self-identification. Here, 
\f0\b Jesus
\f2\b0  declares Himself 
\f0\b "the First and the Last."
\f2\b0 \
This is a significant text. We must read it carefully and honestly, neither overstating nor understating.\

\f0\b What is established:
\f2\b0  The Son takes the LORD's self-identifying title onto Himself. He speaks the Father's own self-disclosure formula.\

\f0\b What is 
\f3\i not
\f0\i0  established:
\f2\b0  That the Son is the Father, or that the Son's "First and Last" identity erases His distinction from the Father, or that the Shema is overthrown.\

\f0\b How are we to understand this consistently with our foundation?
\f2\b0 \
The pattern we have established throughout is that 
\f0\b the Son bears the Father's Name
\f2\b0  (Ex 23:21; John 17:11-12; Phil 2:9). When the Son speaks the LORD's words and bears the LORD's titles, 
\f0\b He does so as the One in whom the Name dwells.
\f2\b0  This is the consistent biblical witness \'97 
\f1\i not
\f2\i0  that the Son is identical to the Father in Person, but that 
\f0\b the Father's Name, glory, and self-disclosure are entrusted to and manifested through the Son.
\f2\b0 \
So when Jesus says 
\f1\i "I am the First and the Last,"
\f2\i0  He is \'97 by the Father's appointment and the Name He bears \'97 exercising the LORD's self-identification as the One in whom the LORD is fully revealed. The Father's "I am the First and the Last" is now spoken through the Son's mouth, because the Son is the Father's full self-expression to the creation.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u950 \u8182 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u951 \u957  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7984 \u948 \u959 \u8058  \u950 \u8182 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Living One \'97 I became dead, and behold I am alive forever and ever."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b This is the decisive distinguishing mark.
\f2\b0  The First and the Last who speaks here is 
\f0\b the One who died and is now alive forevermore
\f2\b0 . The Father did not die. 
\f0\b Only the Son
\f2\b0  can speak these words. So the Son speaks the Father's title as 
\f0\b the One who died for the Father's purposes and was raised to bear His Name forever.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u967 \u969  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u954 \u955 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8069 \u948 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I have the keys of Death and of Hades."
\f2\i0  The Son, by His own death and resurrection, has 
\f0\b been given
\f2\b0  (consistent with our pattern) the keys over death and the unseen realm. This is His present authority.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

