\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 A note of careful observation \'97 Revelation 3:14\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And unto the Angel of the Church of the Laodiceans write, These things saith Amen, the faithful and true witness, that beginning of the creatures of God.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u7969  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8052  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Beginning of the creation of God."
\f2\i0  This title echoes 
\f0\b Proverbs 8:22 LXX
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i "the LORD created/founded me as the beginning of His ways"
\f2\i0 ) and 
\f0\b Colossians 1:15-18
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i "the firstborn of all creation... the beginning, the firstborn from the dead"
\f2\i0 ).\

\f0\b Honest reading per our maxims:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u961 \u967 \u942 
\f2\b0  can mean 
\f1\i "beginning,"
\f2\i0  
\f1\i "first principle,"
\f2\i0  or 
\f1\i "ruler/origin."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  = 
\f1\i "of the creation of God"
\f2\i0  (i.e., of God's creation).\
This title applied to the Son is consistent with what we established carefully: the Son is the one 
\f0\b through whom
\f2\b0  the Father created all things (1 Cor 8:6; Col 1:16; Heb 1:2; John 1:3), the 
\f0\b firstborn over all creation
\f2\b0  (Col 1:15), and so the 
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u961 \u967 \u942 
\f2\b0  \'97 the originating principle and ruler \'97 of the Father's creation.\
This 
\f0\b also
\f2\b0  is consistent with the broader picture of the Son's pre-existence and creative agency that we established by direct witness in our refined study \'97 without requiring the specific identification of Wisdom in Proverbs 8 (which we noted was a parallel, not a witnessed citation).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 4-5 \'97 THE THRONE ROOM AND THE LAMB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is the most theologically loaded vision in the entire Apocalypse for our study. Let us proceed carefully.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Revelation 4 \'97 The Throne of the Father\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And immediately I was ravished in the spirit, and behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat upon the throne. And he that sat, was to look upon, like unto a jasper stone, and a sardine, and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like to an emerald. \'85 And the four beasts had each one of them six wings about him, and they were full of eyes within, and they ceased not day nor night, saying, Holy, holy, holy Lord God almighty, Which Was, and Which Is, and Which Is to come. \'85 Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honour, and power: for thou hast created all things, and for thy will\'92s sake they are, and have been created.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of foundational weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The throne is the Father's throne.
\f2\b0  The One on the throne is identified by the same titles as Rev 1:4, 8: 
\f0\b \uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 , \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come."
\f2\i0  
\f0\b This is the Father.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The worship of the Father is:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "Worthy art Thou... for 
\f3\b Thou hast created all things
\f1\b0 , and 
\f3\b for Thy will's sake
\f1\b0  they are and were created."
\f2\i0 \
The Father is worshipped as the Creator \'97 
\f1\i "for Thy will they were created."
\f2\i0  This is consistent with Isa 44:24 (
\f1\i "I stretched out the heavens alone"
\f2\i0 ) and 1 Cor 8:6 (
\f1\i "the Father, of whom are all things"
\f2\i0 ). 
\f0\b The Father's will is the origin and end of creation.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Revelation 5 \'97 The Lamb Approaches the Throne\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And I saw in the right hand of him that sat upon the throne, a Book written within, and on the backside, sealed with seven seals. And I saw a strong Angel which preached with a loud voice, Who is worthy to open ye 
\f1\i (the)
\f2\i0  book, and to loose the seals thereof? \'85 And one of the Elders said unto me, Weep not: behold, that Lion which is of the tribe of Judah, that root of David, hath obtained to open the Book, and to loose the seven seals thereof. Then I beheld, and lo, in the midst of the throne, and of the four beasts, and in the midst of the Elders, stood a Labe 
\f1\i (Lamb)
\f2\i0  as though he had been killed, \'85 And he came, and took the Book out of the right hand of him that sat upon the throne.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of decisive importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The Lamb is distinct from the One on the throne.
\f2\b0  The Lamb 
\f0\b comes
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b takes
\f2\b0  the scroll 
\f0\b from the right hand of Him who sits on the throne.
\f2\b0  Two distinct figures: the Father on the throne, the Lamb approaching to receive the scroll.\
This is the 
\f0\b fulfillment of Daniel 7:13-14
\f2\b0  \'97 the Son of Man brought before the Ancient of Days to receive dominion. Daniel's vision finds its Apocalyptic counterpart here.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957 \u943 \u954 \u951 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u8001  \u955 \u941 \u969 \u957  \u8001  \u7952 \u954  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u966 \u965 \u955 \u8134 \u962  \u7992 \u959 \u973 \u948 \u945 , \u7969  \u8165 \u943 \u950 \u945  \u916 \u945 \u965 \u943 \u948 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has conquered."
\f2\i0  This fulfills 
\f0\b Genesis 49:9-10
\f2\b0  (the Lion of Judah, the scepter) and 
\f0\b Isaiah 11:1, 10
\f2\b0  (the Root of Jesse / David).\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7944 \u961 \u957 \u943 \u959 \u957  \u7953 \u963 \u964 \u951 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u8033 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u966 \u945 \u947 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "a Lamb standing as having been slain."
\f2\i0  He stands \'97 He is risen. He bears the marks of His slaughter \'97 eternally. The 
\f0\b slain and risen Lamb
\f2\b0  is the eternal form of the exalted Son. This is 
\f0\b the Man Christ Jesus
\f2\b0 , the Mediator, the slain and risen Servant.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Revelation 5:8-14 \'97 The Worship of the Lamb\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And they sung a new song, saying, Thou art worthy to take the Book, and to open the seals thereof, because thou wast killed, and hast redeemed us to God by thy blood out of every kinred 
\f1\i (kindred)
\f2\i0 , and tongue, and people, and nation, And hast made us unto our God Kings and Priests, and we shall reign on the earth. \'85 Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was killed to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and praise. \'85 And all the creatures which are in heaven, and on the earth, and under the earth, and in the sea, and all that are in them, heard I, saying, Praise, and honour, and glory, and power be unto him, that sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb for evermore. And the four beasts said, Amen, and the four and twenty Elders fell down and worshipped him that liveth for evermore.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of supreme importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7968 \u947 \u972 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u945 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u945 \u7989 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u943  \u963 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Thou hast redeemed [us] 
\f3\b to God
\f1\b0  by Thy blood."
\f2\i0  The Lamb's redemption is 
\f0\b for God [the Father]
\f2\b0 . The Lamb purchases people 
\f0\b for the Father.
\f2\b0  Pattern preserved: the Son's work is 
\f0\b unto
\f2\b0  the Father.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to our God."
\f2\i0  The Father is 
\f0\b "our God"
\f2\b0  \'97 the God of the redeemed. The Lamb has made us 
\f0\b kings and priests to His God and Father
\f2\b0  (cf. Rev 1:6).\

\f0\b (3) The doxology of v. 13
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to Him that sits on the throne AND to the Lamb"
\f2\i0  \'97 combines the worship of the Father and the Son. 
\f0\b Two distinct figures
\f2\b0 , but 
\f0\b joint recipients of the eternal blessing, honor, glory, and dominion.
\f2\b0 \
This is the same pattern as Rev 22:1, 3 \'97 
\f0\b the throne of God and of the Lamb
\f2\b0  \'97 preserved throughout: the Father on the throne, the Lamb beside Him, jointly receiving worship.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 REVELATION 7:9-17 \'97 THE LAMB IN THE MIDST OF THE THRONE\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 After these things I beheld, and lo, a great multitude, \'85 stood before the throne, and before the Lamb, \'85 and they cried with a loud voice, saying, Salvation cometh of our God, that sitteth upon the throne, and of the Lamb. \'85 Therefore are they in the presence of the throne of God, and serve him day and night in his Temple, and he that sitteth on the throne, will dwell among them. They shall hunger no more, neither thirst any more, neither shall the sun light on them, neither any heat. For the Lamb, which is in the midst of the throne, shall govern them, and shall lead them unto the lively fountains of waters, and God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7977  \u963 \u969 \u964 \u951 \u961 \u943 \u945  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ... \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8183  \u7944 \u961 \u957 \u943 \u8179 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Salvation belongs to our God... and to the Lamb."
\f2\i0  Joint attribution. Salvation comes from the Father and the Lamb together.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056  \u7944 \u961 \u957 \u943 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u8056  \u7936 \u957 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u963 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Lamb in the midst of the throne."
\f2\i0  This is a striking phrase. The Lamb is 
\f0\b in the middle of the throne
\f2\b0  \'97 closely associated with it, sharing its center. Yet 
\f0\b the Father is the One sitting on the throne
\f2\b0  (v. 15), and the Lamb is distinct from Him. The Lamb shares the throne's center because He is at the Father's right hand \'97 the place of supreme honor and shared rule.\
This will become explicit in Rev 22:1, 3 \'97 
\f1\i "the throne of God and of the Lamb"
\f2\i0  \'97 a single throne, jointly occupied.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u958 \u945 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u968 \u949 \u953  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u960 \u8118 \u957  \u948 \u940 \u954 \u961 \u965 \u959 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "God shall wipe away every tear."
\f2\i0  The Father Himself, through His ministering presence, comforts His people in the eternal state.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Son in the Apocalypse \'97 Revelation 19:11-16: The Returning King; Revelation 21:5-7: The One on the Throne Speaks; Revelation 22:12-13 and 22:16: A Careful Textual Examination with the Typological Principle; Revelation 22:1-5: The Throne of God and of the Lamb; Revelation 22:7, 20: The Final Words; the Grand Synthesis \'97 the Son in the Apocalypse; Where the Study Stands\
REVELATION 19:11-16 \'97 THE RETURNING KING\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And I saw heaven open, and behold, a white horse, and he that sat upon him, was called, Faithful and true, and he judgeth and fighteth righteously. And his eyes were as a flame of fire, and on his head were many crowns: and he had a name written, that no man knew but himself. And he was clothed with a garment dipt 
\f1\i (the Geneva prints "dipt")
\f2\i0  in blood, and his name is called THE WORD OF GOD. \'85 And he hath upon his garment, and upon his thigh a name written, THE KINGS 
\f1\i (KING)
\f2\i0  OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of supreme importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u928 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7944 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Faithful and True."
\f2\i0  The titles of Rev 3:14.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u967 \u969 \u957  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945  \u947 \u949 \u947 \u961 \u945 \u956 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u8003  \u959 \u8016 \u948 \u949 \u8054 \u962  \u959 \u7990 \u948 \u949 \u957  \u949 \u7984  \u956 \u8052  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "having a name written that no one knows except Himself."
\f2\i0  This is significant. The Son has a Name 
\f0\b known only to Himself
\f2\b0 . There is depth to His Person that remains hidden even at His return.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u941 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "His Name is called: the Word of God."
\f2\i0 \
This is 
\f0\b the explicit identification of the Returning King with "the Word of God"
\f2\b0  \'97 directly tying back to John 1:1 (
\f1\i "In the beginning was the Word"
\f2\i0 ). The Lamb who is the Word \'97 the Father's self-expression, His creative speech, His final message to the creation \'97 comes in judgment.\
Note: 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Word of God"
\f2\i0  \'97 uses the genitive: 
\f0\b the Word 
\f3\i of God
\f2\i0\b0  \'97 i.e., 
\f0\b the Word belonging to / from / of God [the Father].
\f2\b0  The Son is the Father's Word \'97 never independent, always proceeding from and bearing the Father's mind.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u914 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u8058 \u962  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u941 \u969 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u969 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "King of kings and Lord of lords."
\f2\i0  This title is also given to the Father in 
