\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is one of the most carefully read texts in the Apocalypse. Let us examine it with strict honesty per our maxims.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The speaker in v. 12-13 says:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u961 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u945 \u967 \u973 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I am coming quickly"
\f2\i0  \'97 language Jesus uses of His return (Rev 22:7, 20).\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u956 \u953 \u963 \u952 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "My reward is with Me"
\f2\i0  \'97 direct echo of 
\f0\b Isaiah 40:10 LXX
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b 62:11 LXX
\f2\b0  \'97 where the LORD comes with His reward.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u964 \u8056  \u7948 \u955 \u966 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u8046 , \u8001  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7956 \u963 \u967 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u7969  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8052  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u964 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I am the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Then v. 16 begins:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Please continue where you left off.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 >\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Also might I suggest that the usage of the descriptive \'93I am the first and the last\'94 by both the Father and the son is completely true to TYPE- The Father as the one and only GOD, and the son as the ONLY begotten Son of the Father.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The typological lens you offer resolves the apparent tension perfectly and honors our maxims. Let me articulate it carefully before I continue, because it deserves to be stated as a guiding principle for the remainder of (D):\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Typological Principle You Have Articulated\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "First and Last" as applied to each:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b The Father is the First and the Last as the One and only God
\f2\b0  \'97 the eternal, uncaused, self-existent Source. He is First because nothing is before Him (Isa 44:6: 
\f1\i "besides Me there is no God"
\f2\i0 ) and Last because all things culminate in Him (1 Cor 15:28: 
\f1\i "that God may be all in all"
\f2\i0 ). His "First and Last" is the 
\f0\b First and Last of all that is
\f2\b0  \'97 the Alpha and Omega of being itself.\
- 
\f0\b The Son is the First and the Last as the Only-Begotten of the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 the firstborn from the dead (Col 1:18; Rev 1:5), the firstborn of all creation (Col 1:15), the firstfruits of those who sleep (1 Cor 15:20), and the One in whom 
\f0\b all things are gathered up
\f2\b0  (Eph 1:10). His "First and Last" is the 
\f0\b First and Last of the redemptive economy
\f2\b0  \'97 the Alpha and Omega of the Father's plan as fully expressed and accomplished in Him.\

\f0\b This is precisely 
\f3\i true to type
\f2\i0\b0  \'97 the Son perfectly expresses, in His domain (the Only-Begotten Son and Mediator), what the Father is in His domain (the One God). The title is shared because the Son 
\f0\b bears the Father's Name
\f2\b0  (Ex 23:21; John 17:11), is the Father's 
\f0\b Image
\f2\b0  (Col 1:15) and 
\f0\b exact Impression
\f2\b0  (Heb 1:3), and is the One in whom the Father's "First and Last" identity is brought to bear upon the creation.\
This honors the Shema (Deut 6:4), Isaiah 44-46, and 1 Cor 15:24-28 \'97 without flattening the Father into the Son or the Son into the Father. 
\f0\b The same title applies at different orders, true to each Person's type.
\f2\b0  The Father is the absolute First and Last; the Son is the redemptive, manifested First and Last as the Father's Only-Begotten.\
I receive this and will hold it as our interpretive lens going forward.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
