\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What Is Decisively Established by the Apocalypse\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 (1) The Father remains the One God on the throne throughout.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The throne is His (Rev 4-5; 7; 21; 22).\
- He is 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 
\f2\b0  \'97 the Almighty \'97 throughout (Rev 1:8; 4:8; 11:17; 15:3; 16:7; 19:6; 21:22).\
- He is 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 the eternally being One (Rev 1:4, 8; 4:8).\
- He is worshipped as the Creator (Rev 4:11).\
- He gives the revelation to His Son (Rev 1:1).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 (2) The Son shares the Father's titles "true to type" \'97 as the Only-Begotten.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Per your beautifully articulated principle: 
\f0\b the Father is First and Last as the One God; the Son is First and Last as the Only-Begotten.
\f2\b0  Each title applied to the Son in the Apocalypse reflects His role as 
\f0\b the manifestation, image, and full self-expression of the Father to and within the creation
\f2\b0  \'97 never as a rival, never as a second God, never displacing the Father's unique supremacy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 (3) The Lamb retains His humanity forever \'97 as the slain and risen Man Christ Jesus.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 He is 
\f0\b the Lamb as having been slain
\f2\b0  (Rev 5:6) \'97 eternally. He is 
\f0\b like a Son of Man
\f2\b0  in His glorified appearance (Rev 1:13). He is 
\f0\b the Man Christ Jesus
\f2\b0  as the one Mediator (1 Tim 2:5). The redeemed are forever in the presence of the slain and risen Lamb, who bears the marks of His suffering and through whom the Father is known.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 (4) The consummation is the joint reign of God and the Lamb \'97 the Father supreme, the Son at His right hand \'97 true to the eternal order Paul articulated in 1 Cor 15:28.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The throne is one. The worship is one. The Name is one. The Light is one \'97 the Father's glory shining through the Lamb to illuminate the eternal city. This is the consummation we examined in (C), now visualized in the Apocalypse: 
\f0\b God all in all, through His Beloved Son, with the redeemed gathered into the Father's presence through the Lamb's mediation.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 (5) The Apocalypse gathers every prophetic thread from Genesis to the consummation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 From 
\f0\b Gen 3:15
\f2\b0  (the seed of the woman who crushes the serpent \'97 fulfilled in Rev 12 and 20) to 
\f0\b Gen 22
\f2\b0  (the beloved Son as Lamb \'97 fulfilled in the slain Lamb of Rev 5) to 
\f0\b Gen 49:10
\f2\b0  (the Lion of Judah \'97 Rev 5:5) to 
\f0\b Num 24:17
\f2\b0  (the Star \'97 Rev 22:16) to 
\f0\b Ps 2 and 110
\f2\b0  (the Anointed at the right hand \'97 Rev 1, 5, 22) to 
\f0\b Dan 7
\f2\b0  (the Son of Man before the Ancient of Days \'97 Rev 1, 5) to 
\f0\b Isa 53
\f2\b0  (the slain Lamb \'97 Rev 5, 13) to 
\f0\b Zech 12:10
\f2\b0  (the pierced One \'97 Rev 1:7) to 
\f0\b Mal 4:2
\f2\b0  (the Sun of Righteousness \'97 Rev 22:16 the Morning Star) \'97 
\f0\b every thread is gathered.
\f2\b0 \
The Apocalypse is the 
\f0\b canonical consummation
\f2\b0  of all prophecy concerning the Person of Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Where Our Study Now Stands\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We have completed (A), (B), (C), and (D). Per your direction, two crowning themes remain \'97 and these will complete and crown the entire study:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 NEXT \'97 Part E: The Nature and Essence of the Father as Eternal Spirit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is essential and will clarify many things:\
- John 4:24 \'97 
\f0\b "God is Spirit"
\f2\b0  \'97 His fundamental Nature\
- The implications for the "singular throne" you have rightly noted\
- The Father's omnipresence as Spirit, not confined to a location\
- The relation of the Father (Spirit) to the Son (Image, Word made flesh, Man at the right hand)\
- The eternal Spirit and the seven Spirits before the throne \'97 what can be honestly said\
- How the Father's Spirit-Nature undergirds His invisibility (John 1:18; 1 Tim 6:16) and yet His presence in all things\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 THEN \'97 Part F: The Indwelling \'97 That We Should Be the Habitation of God in Christ\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is the crowning glory of the entire revelation:\
- John 17:20-23 \'97 
\f1\i "that they may be one, even as We are one... I in them, and Thou in Me"
\f2\i0 \
- John 14:23 \'97 
\f1\i "We will come unto him, and make Our abode with him"
\f2\i0 \
- The Father's purpose: that the elect become the habitation of the Father through the Son by the Spirit\
- Ephesians 3:14-19 \'97 
\f1\i "that ye might be filled with all the fullness of God"
\f2\i0 \
- 2 Corinthians 6:16 \'97 
\f1\i "I will dwell in them, and walk in them"
\f2\i0 \
- The Bride and the Bridegroom \'97 the consummation of the indwelling\
- Rev 21:3 \'97 
\f1\i "the tabernacle of God is with men, and He will dwell with them"
\f2\i0  \'97 the final fulfillment\
Shall we proceed to 
\f0\b (E) \'97 the Nature and Essence of the Father as Eternal Spirit
\f2\b0  \'97 which will properly prepare us for the indwelling theme in (F)?\
