\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Direct Witness \'97 John 4:24\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "God is a Spirit, and they that worship him, must worship him in spirit and truth."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Spirit is God"
\f2\i0  (the predicate 
\f0\b \uc0\u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945 
\f2\b0  is placed first for emphasis). This is 
\f0\b Jesus' own direct statement
\f2\b0  about the Father's essential Nature.\
Note the careful grammar: 
\f0\b \uc0\u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945 
\f2\b0  is anarthrous (no article) \'97 qualitative \'97 telling us 
\f0\b what God is in His essence
\f2\b0 , not identifying Him as one Spirit among others. 
\f0\b The Father is Spirit by nature
\f2\b0  \'97 that is His fundamental essence.\
This is spoken to the Samaritan woman in the context of Jesus distinguishing 
\f0\b true worship
\f2\b0  from worship located in a specific place (Mount Gerizim or Jerusalem). His point: 
\f0\b the Father is not confined to a geographic location
\f2\b0  because 
\f0\b He is Spirit
\f2\b0  \'97 and therefore must be worshipped 
\f0\b in spirit and truth
\f2\b0 , not by being approached in a particular place.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 1 Timothy 1:17\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Now unto the King everlasting, immortal, invisible, unto God only wise, be honour and glory, for ever, and ever, Amen."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Father is described as:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u914 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u8058 \u962  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u974 \u957 \u969 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "King of the ages"
\f2\i0  \'97 eternal in dominion.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u966 \u952 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "incorruptible / immortal"
\f2\i0  \'97 not subject to decay or change.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u972 \u961 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "invisible"
\f2\i0  \'97 cannot be seen.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the only God"
\f2\i0  \'97 preserving the Shema (cf. John 17:3 \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u957 
\f2\b0 ).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Two witnesses now agree on a key point:
\f2\b0  the Father is 
\f0\b invisible
\f2\b0  because 
\f0\b He is Spirit
\f2\b0 . Spirit is, by its nature, not visible to physical sight.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 1 Timothy 6:15-16\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Which in due time he shall show, that is blessed and Prince only, the King of Kings and Lord of Lords, Who only hath immortality, and dwelleth in the light that none can attain unto, whom never man saw, neither can see, unto whom be honour and power everlasting, Amen."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Father is:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u7956 \u967 \u969 \u957  \u7936 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u945 \u963 \u943 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the only One having immortality."
\f2\i0  This is a strong statement \'97 the Father alone has immortality as His own essential possession.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u966 \u8182 \u962  \u959 \u7984 \u954 \u8182 \u957  \u7936 \u960 \u961 \u972 \u963 \u953 \u964 \u959 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "dwelling in unapproachable light."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8003 \u957  \u949 \u7990 \u948 \u949 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u948 \u949 \u8054 \u962  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u969 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u948 \u8050  \u7984 \u948 \u949 \u8150 \u957  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "whom no man has seen, nor can see."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Three witnesses now establish:
\f2\b0  the Father is 
\f0\b invisible
\f2\b0  (John 1:18; 1 Tim 1:17; 1 Tim 6:16). And the reason is His essential Nature: 
\f0\b He is Spirit, dwelling in unapproachable light.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 OT Foundation \'97 The Father as Spirit\
Genesis 1:2 LXX:\
NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Yet the earth was invisible and unformed, and darkness was over the abyss, and a divine wind was being carried along over the water. \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 1:2 LXX, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (the NETS renders \uc0\u960 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  "a divine wind"; the 1599 Geneva reads: "\'85and the Spirit of God moved upon the waters.")
\f2\i0 \
The Spirit of God is present at creation \'97 active, moving, hovering. This is 
\f0\b the Father's own Spirit
\f2\b0  \'97 not a separate Person in the post-Nicene sense (which we have set aside per maxim #3), but 
\f0\b the Father's own essential being and active presence
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
