\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 WHAT THE TEXT STRICTLY ESTABLISHES\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Per our maxims, let us note exactly what the text says \'97 no more, no less:\
1. 
\f0\b There are "seven Spirits"
\f2\b0  \'97 designated as such.\
2. 
\f0\b They are "of God"
\f2\b0  \'97 belonging to / from the Father.\
3. 
\f0\b They are "before the throne"
\f2\b0  \'97 positioned in the Father's presence.\
4. 
\f0\b The Son "has" them
\f2\b0  (Rev 3:1) \'97 He possesses or holds them.\
5. 
\f0\b They are visually represented as seven burning lamps
\f2\b0  (Rev 4:5).\
6. 
\f0\b They are also visually represented as the Lamb's seven eyes
\f2\b0  (Rev 5:6).\
7. 
\f0\b They are sent into all the earth
\f2\b0  (Rev 5:6).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

