\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Single Pattern Preserved Throughout:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - 
\f0\b The Father is the Source.
\f2\b0  The Spirit is His; the promise is His; the giving is from Him.\
- 
\f0\b The Son is the Agent.
\f2\b0  He receives from the Father; He dispenses to the people.\
- 
\f0\b The Spirit is the Father's own essential Spirit-presence
\f2\b0  \'97 now extended through the Son to the redeemed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What This Honors:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - 
\f0\b The Shema
\f2\b0  \'97 One God, the Father (Deut 6:4; John 17:3; 1 Cor 8:6; 1 Tim 2:5).\
- 
\f0\b Isaiah 44-46
\f2\b0  \'97 the Father acts alone, by His Word, by His Spirit, but without rival Deity.\
- 
\f0\b John 4:24
\f2\b0  \'97 the Father is Spirit by Nature.\
- 
\f0\b 1 Cor 15:24-28
\f2\b0  \'97 the Son delivers the Kingdom to the Father, and the Son Himself is subjected to the Father, that God may be all in all.\
- 
\f0\b Mark 13:32 / Acts 1:7
\f2\b0  \'97 the Father alone knows the times; the Son depends on the Father even in His exalted state.\
- 
\f0\b Phil 2:9-11
\f2\b0  \'97 the Son's name is given by the Father, and all confession of Him is to the Father's glory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What This Avoids:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The post-Nicene flattening of the Father, Son, and Spirit into "three co-equal Persons of one substance" \'97 a metaphysical formulation Scripture does not deliver.\
- The notion that the Spirit is a separate "third Person of the Godhead" eternally distinct from the Father \'97 Scripture consistently calls the Spirit 
\f0\b "the Spirit OF God,"
\f2\b0  
\f0\b "the Spirit OF the Father,"
\f2\b0  
\f0\b "the Spirit OF Christ,"
\f2\b0  
\f0\b "the Holy Spirit of promise"
\f2\b0  \'97 always as 
\f0\b someone's
\f2\b0  Spirit, never as a free-standing third Deity.\
- The error of denying the Son's pre-existence or His true reception of the Father's Spirit at exaltation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A FINAL OBSERVATION \'97 THE BEAUTY OF ACTS 2:33\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 What Acts 2:33 reveals is breathtaking when we hold the whole picture:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Father, who is Eternal Spirit, indwelt His Son fully during His earthly ministry. The Son, in obedience, accomplished the Father's will to the point of death on the cross. The Father raised the Son and exalted Him to His right hand. There, the Son received the Father's promised Spirit \'97 the same Spirit that had indwelt Him in His earthly life \'97 now to be dispensed through Him to all who believe.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b The Son, then, pours forth the Spirit \'97 the Father's own essential Presence \'97 upon His Church, so that the Father may dwell in the redeemed in the same way He dwelt in the Son.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b This is the entire arc of redemption: the Father, by His Spirit, in His Son, indwelling His people.
\f2\b0 \
And this is precisely the indwelling we will now examine in Part F \'97 where Jesus prays 
\f1\i "that they all may be one, as Thou Father art in Me, and I in Thee, that they also may be one in Us"
\f2\i0  (John 17:21).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 READY TO PROCEED TO PART F\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Acts 2:33 is now properly understood as 
\f0\b the hinge
\f2\b0  between:\
- The Father-Son union of Jesus' earthly ministry (Part E).\
- The indwelling of the redeemed by the Father through the Son by the Spirit (Part F).\
Shall we now proceed to 
\f0\b Part F \'97 The Indwelling: That We Should Be the Habitation of God in Christ
\f2\b0  \'97 beginning with 
\f0\b John 14:16-23 (the Father and Son coming to make Their abode)
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b John 17:20-26 (the High Priestly Prayer for our oneness in Them)
\f2\b0 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 I understand that in Old Testament times YHVH\'92s Spirit came \'93upon\'94 certain individuals and acted upon them to prophesy and to perform miracles. This Spirit may abide upon them, and in some cases it departed from them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 >\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Presently, we are told, that the Spirit, enters INTO the elect- never to depart\'85 for the Gifts and Callings of God are without repentance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Yes \'97 this is a profoundly important distinction, and it sets up Part F beautifully. You have identified one of the most significant shifts in redemptive history. Let me address it carefully per our maxims, examining the witnesses in both Testaments and seeing what the Word itself establishes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b THE SHIFT IN THE SPIRIT'S OPERATION \'97 FROM "UPON" TO "WITHIN"
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 PART 1 \'97 THE OT PATTERN: THE SPIRIT "UPON," "MIGHTILY UPON," AND DEPARTING\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The OT consistently presents the Spirit's operation in terms of 
\f0\b coming upon
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b resting upon
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b clothing
\f2\b0 , and sometimes 
\f0\b departing
\f2\b0  \'97 generally tied to specific tasks, callings, or seasons.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Spirit Came Upon \'97 Specific Persons for Specific Tasks\
Numbers 11:25 LXX (Moses and the seventy elders):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And the Lord came down in a cloud and spoke to him and took away some of the spirit that was upon him and put it upon the seventy men who were elders. Now as the spirit rested upon them, they also prophesied, and they no longer added. \'97 
\f0\b Numbers 11:25, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The Spirit is 
\f0\b upon (\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u943 )
\f2\b0  Moses.\
- A portion is 
\f0\b taken from (\uc0\u7936 \u960 \u972 )
\f2\b0  that Spirit and 
\f0\b placed upon (\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u943 )
\f2\b0  the seventy.\
- When the Spirit 
\f0\b rested upon
\f2\b0  them, they prophesied.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Spirit is depictable as a portion that can be transferred
\f2\b0  \'97 a remarkable image of the Spirit's external operation upon chosen vessels for the task at hand.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Judges 6:34 LXX (Gideon):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And a divine spirit entered Gedeon 
\f1\i (Gideon)
\f2\i0 , and he sounded with a horn and called out for Abiezer after him. \'97 
\f0\b Judges 6:34, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The LXX uses 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957 \u941 \u948 \u965 \u963 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "clothed"
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Spirit of the LORD clothed Gideon."
\f2\i0  The Hebrew (preserved in the Geneva from the Hebrew) is even more vivid: the Spirit 
\f1\i "clothed itself with" / "put on"
\f2\i0  Gideon. He becomes the garment, the vessel, the form the Spirit takes on for the task.\
This is 
\f0\b the Spirit operating from without, taking a man as its instrument.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Judges 14:6, 19; 15:14 LXX (Samson):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And a spirit of the Lord made straight for him, and he tore it apart as he would tear apart a kid of goats, and there was nothing in his hand. And he did not tell his father or mother what he had done.\'85And a spirit of the Lord made straight for him, and he went down to Ascalon. And from there he struck down thirty men and took their robes and gave them to those who had told the problem. And Sampson 
\f1\i (Samson)
\f2\i0  was furiously angry, and he went back to his father\'92s house.\'85And they came as far as Jawbone, and the allophyles 
\f1\i (the Philistines)
\f2\i0  shouted in triumph and ran to meet him, and a spirit of the Lord leapt upon him, and the cords that were on his arms became like flax which was burnt by fire, and his bonds melted from his hands. \'97 
\f0\b Judges 14:6, 19; 15:14 (ellipsis), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u7973 \u955 \u945 \u964 \u959  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Spirit leaped upon him."
\f2\i0  Sudden, powerful, external visitation for the moment of need \'97 and then departing. Samson's life shows the Spirit's recurring visits for specific feats, not a continuous indwelling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1 Samuel 10:6, 10 LXX (Saul):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 and a spirit of the Lord will spring upon you, and you will prophesy along with them and be turned into another man. \'97 
\f0\b 1 Samuel 10:6, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Spirit Departed From Saul \'97 1 Samuel 16:14 LXX:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And a spirit of the Lord departed from Saoul 
\f1\i (Saul)
\f2\i0 , and an evil spirit from the Lord tormented him. \'97 
\f0\b 1 Samuel 16:14, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Spirit of the LORD departed (\uc0\u7936 \u960 \u941 \u963 \u964 \u951  \u7936 \u960 \u972 ) from Saul.
\f2\b0  This is the explicit textual witness to 
\f0\b a real departure of the Spirit
\f2\b0  from a man upon whom the Spirit had previously come.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 David's Prayer After His Sin \'97 Psalm 50:11 LXX (Ps 51:11 MT):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Do not cast me away from your face, and your holy spirit do not take from me. \'97 
\f0\b Psalm 50:13 LXX (= Ps 51:11 MT), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of critical importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 David himself prays that the Spirit not be taken from him
\f2\b0  \'97 having seen what happened to Saul. This is the OT believer's anxious consciousness: 
\f0\b the Spirit's presence is something that can be withdrawn.
\f2\b0  David did not have the kind of certainty Paul speaks of in Eph 1:13-14 (the sealing of the Spirit unto the day of redemption).\
This single verse is decisive: 
\f0\b in the OT economy, the Spirit's presence with a believer was something to be prayed for, not something assured by sealing.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Other OT Examples of the Spirit Coming Upon:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - 
\f0\b Bezalel
\f2\b0  for craftsmanship \'97 Ex 31:3 LXX: 
\f1\i "\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957 \u941 \u960 \u955 \u951 \u963 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u952 \u949 \u8150 \u959 \u957 ..."
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "and I have filled him with the divine Spirit."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b The Prophets
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Spirit of the LORD spoke by me"
\f2\i0  (2 Sam 23:2).\
- 
\f0\b Othniel
\f2\b0  \'97 Judg 3:10: 
\f1\i "the Spirit of the LORD was upon him."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Jephthah
\f2\b0  \'97 Judg 11:29: 
\f1\i "the Spirit of the LORD came upon Jephthah."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Ezekiel
\f2\b0  \'97 the Spirit entered him and lifted him (Ezek 2:2; 3:24; etc.) \'97 but in the context of prophetic vision, not permanent indwelling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The OT Pattern Summarized\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 In the OT economy, the Spirit of the LORD:\
1. 
\f0\b Came upon (\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u943 )
\f2\b0  chosen individuals for specific tasks or seasons.\
2. 
\f0\b Could depart
\f2\b0  from them (1 Sam 16:14).\
3. 
\f0\b Could be prayed to remain
\f2\b0  (Ps 51:11).\
4. 
\f0\b Was generally task-oriented
\f2\b0  \'97 prophecy, judging, kingship, craftsmanship, prophetic vision.\
5. 
\f0\b Was not a permanent, sealing, indwelling presence
\f2\b0  for the believer generally.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 PART 2 \'97 THE PROMISED NEW COVENANT: THE SPIRIT WITHIN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The OT prophets themselves foresaw a coming change \'97 a day when the Spirit's operation would shift from "upon" to "within."\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Ezekiel 36:26-27 LXX \'97 The Foundational Promise\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And I will give you a new heart, and a new spirit I will give in you, and I will remove the stone heart from your flesh and give you a heart of flesh. And I will give my spirit in you and will act so that you walk in my statutes and keep my judgments and perform them. \'97 
\f0\b Ezekiel 36:26-27, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of decisive importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u940  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u948 \u974 \u963 \u969  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I will give My Spirit 
\f3\b within you
\f1\b0 ."
\f2\i0 \
Note carefully the preposition: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "within / in you."
\f2\i0  This is 
\f0\b not "upon"
\f2\b0  (\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u943 ). This is the radical promise of the New Covenant: the LORD's Spirit will be 
\f0\b placed within
\f2\b0  His people.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  This is paired with 
\f0\b a new heart and a new spirit
\f2\b0  \'97 an internal transformation, not an external visitation.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  The result is 
\f0\b walking in His statutes and keeping His judgments
\f2\b0  \'97 the law internalized, just as Jeremiah 31:31-34 LXX (Jer 38:31-34 LXX) promised the law written on the heart, not on stone.\

