\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He dwells with you, and shall be in you."
\f2\i0  The Geneva captures the precise distinction:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i present tense
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "He dwells with you"
\f2\i0  (currently \'97 alongside, in the Son's presence among them).\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i future tense
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "He shall be 
\f3\b in
\f1\b0  you"
\f2\i0  (coming \'97 to indwell them).\

\f0\b This is Jesus' own announcement of the shift from "with/upon" to "within."
\f2\b0  The Spirit was currently with them (because He was in Jesus, who was with them) \'97 but He would soon be 
\f0\b in them.
