\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of decisive importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u963 \u966 \u961 \u945 \u947 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u8183  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "you were sealed with the Spirit."
\f2\i0  The aorist passive \'97 a 
\f0\b definitive past action
\f2\b0 . The believer 
\f0\b has been sealed
\f2\b0 . This is not a process that can be undone.\

\f0\b (2) The seal (\uc0\u963 \u966 \u961 \u945 \u947 \u943 \u962 )
\f2\b0  in ancient practice was a 
\f0\b mark of ownership, authentication, and security.
\f2\b0  A sealed item could not be opened without breaking the seal \'97 and breaking the king's seal was a capital offense. The Spirit's sealing means 
\f0\b the believer is marked as belonging to God, authenticated as His, and secure unto the day of redemption.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u961 \u961 \u945 \u946 \u8060 \u957  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u943 \u945 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the earnest / down-payment of our inheritance."
\f2\i0  The Spirit is the 
\f0\b first installment
\f2\b0  of our full inheritance \'97 guaranteeing the rest. An earnest is 
\f0\b never reclaimed
\f2\b0  by the giver; it secures the future delivery.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u955 \u973 \u964 \u961 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "unto the redemption"
\f2\i0  \'97 the sealing is 
\f0\b unto
\f2\b0  the future full redemption. The Spirit is given 
\f0\b to remain until
\f2\b0  the day of complete redemption.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

