\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 PART 4 \'97 THE FOUNDATIONAL DIFFERENCE: WHY THIS CHANGE?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The key question is: 
\f0\b why did the Spirit's operation change from "upon and possibly departing" to "within and permanent"?
\f2\b0 \
The answer is given explicitly by Jesus:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 John 7:39 (Greek):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 \'85for the holy Ghost was not yet given, because that Jesus was not yet glorified \'97 
\f0\b John 7:39 (ellipsis), 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 John 16:7 (Greek):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Yet I tell you the truth, It is expedient for you that I go away: for if I go not away, that Comforter will not come unto you: but if I depart, I will send him unto you. \'97 
\f0\b John 16:7, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Son's glorification (death, resurrection, ascension, enthronement) was the prerequisite for the indwelling Spirit's bestowal.
\f2\b0  Why?\
1. 
\f0\b The Father's Spirit could not indwell sinful humans
\f2\b0  until sin was atoned for (Heb 9:14, 22; 10:14).\
2. 
\f0\b The Spirit's indwelling is dependent on the Son's mediatorial work.
\f2\b0  The Son had to 
\f1\i finish the work
\f2\i0  (John 17:4), 
\f1\i purge our sins
\f2\i0  (Heb 1:3), and 
\f1\i enter the heavenly Holy Place
\f2\i0  (Heb 9:24) before the Spirit could be given to dwell in believers.\
3. 
\f0\b Once the Son was glorified, He received the Spirit from the Father
\f2\b0  (Acts 2:33 \'97 examined just before this) 
\f0\b and poured Him forth
\f2\b0  upon His Church.\

\f0\b The OT saints could not have the indwelling Spirit because the Son had not yet been glorified.
\f2\b0  The OT economy was 
\f0\b anticipatory
\f2\b0  \'97 the Spirit could come 
\f1\i upon
\f2\i0  saints for tasks, but could not 
\f1\i indwell
\f2\i0  them as a sealing presence until the Son's work was complete.\
This is why John 7:39 is so emphatic: 
\f0\b the Spirit was not yet given
\f2\b0  \'97 \uc0\u959 \u8020 \u960 \u969  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7974 \u957  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \'97 because Jesus was not yet glorified.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

