\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A CRUCIAL NUANCE \'97 DAVID'S PRAYER vs. PAUL'S DECLARATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Compare side by side:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 David (under the OT economy):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Psalm 50:11 LXX (51:11):
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u940  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u8056  \u7949 \u947 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u956 \u8052  \u7936 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u957 \u941 \u955 \u8131 \u962  \u7936 \u960 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166 "
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "Take not Thy Holy Spirit from me."
\f2\i0 \
A 
\f0\b prayer of anxious dependence
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i please do not withdraw what may be withdrawn.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Paul (under the NT economy):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Ephesians 4:30:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "\uc0\u7952 \u963 \u966 \u961 \u945 \u947 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u945 \u957  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u955 \u965 \u964 \u961 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962 "
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "you were sealed unto the day of redemption."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Romans 11:29:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "\uc0\u7936 \u956 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u956 \u941 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u945  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u964 \u8048  \u967 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7969  \u954 \u955 \u8134 \u963 \u953 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 "
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f1\i "the gifts and calling of God are without repentance."
\f2\i0 \
A 
\f0\b declaration of certain possession
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i you have been definitively sealed; what has been given will not be revoked.
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b The difference is staggering, and it reflects the difference in the two economies.
\f2\b0  David could only pray; the post-Pentecost believer is 
\f1\i assured
\f2\i0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A NECESSARY CAUTION \'97 GRIEVING vs. LOSING\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 While the indwelling is permanent, the NT does warn that the Spirit can be 
\f0\b grieved
\f2\b0  (Eph 4:30: 
\f1\i "grieve not the Holy Spirit of God"
\f2\i0 ) and 
\f0\b quenched
\f2\b0  (1 Thess 5:19: 
\f1\i "quench not the Spirit"
\f2\i0 ). But notice:\
- 
\f0\b Grieving and quenching are not the same as departing.
\f2\b0 \
- The believer can 
\f0\b cause the Spirit sorrow
\f2\b0  by sin (grieving) and can 
\f0\b stifle the Spirit's operation
\f2\b0  by disobedience (quenching).\
- But 
\f0\b the Spirit remains
\f2\b0  \'97 sealed unto the day of redemption.\
The OT saint risked the Spirit's departure for sin. The NT saint, while seriously cautioned not to grieve or quench the Spirit, 
\f0\b does not face the prospect of the Spirit's departure
\f2\b0 , because the basis of the indwelling is no longer the saint's qualification, but the Son's completed work and the Father's irrevocable sealing.\
This is the radical security of the New Covenant.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 PART 6 \'97 WHY THIS IS THE GROUNDWORK FOR PART F\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 What you have identified is precisely the doctrinal foundation needed for 
\f0\b Part F \'97 The Indwelling.
\f2\b0 \
Because:\
1. 
\f0\b In the OT, no human could be the "habitation of God"
\f2\b0  in any complete, permanent sense \'97 the Spirit could come upon, but not indwell permanently. The temple was the symbolic dwelling, but even it could be forsaken (Ezek 10).\
2. 
\f0\b In the NT, the believer himself becomes the temple of the Holy Spirit
\f2\b0  (1 Cor 3:16-17; 6:19; 2 Cor 6:16) \'97 because the Spirit now indwells. 
\f0\b The believer is the new temple.
\f2\b0 \
3. 
\f0\b This is only possible because:
\f2\b0 \
- The Son was glorified.\
- The Spirit was given by the Father through the Son.\
- The believer is now sealed forever \'97 bearing the Father's own indwelling Presence.\
4. 
\f0\b The promise of John 14:23
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "We will come unto him, and make Our abode with him"
\f2\i0  \'97 refers to both the Father and the Son making the believer Their dwelling through the Spirit. 
\f0\b This was not possible in the OT economy.
\f2\b0  It is possible 
\f1\i now
\f2\i0 , because the Son has been glorified and the Spirit has been poured out.\
5. 
\f0\b The High Priestly Prayer of John 17:20-26
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "that they all may be one, as Thou Father art in Me, and I in Thee, that they also may be one in Us"
\f2\i0  \'97 describes a 
\f0\b mutual indwelling
\f2\b0  that 
\f1\i requires
\f2\i0  the permanent presence of the Spirit. The OT saint could not enter into this; the NT saint can, because of what you have rightly identified.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A FINAL OBSERVATION \'97 THE GLORY OF YOUR INSIGHT\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 What you have noted is one of the most consequential differences in all of redemptive history \'97 and it is exactly what makes the New Covenant 
\f0\b new
\f2\b0 .\
The Father, who is Eternal Spirit, 
\f0\b could not
\f2\b0  indwell sinful man fully and permanently until the Son's atoning work was completed and the Son was glorified. The OT saints lived in faith and looked forward; the Spirit could come upon them for specific tasks and even rest mightily on them. But the 
\f1\i permanent indwelling
\f2\i0  of the Father by His Spirit, sealing the believer unto the day of redemption \'97 this was reserved for the era after the Son's glorification.\
Pentecost is the 
\f0\b inauguration of this new reality.
\f2\b0  From Pentecost forward, the elect are not merely 
\f1\i visited
\f2\i0  by God's Spirit \'97 they are 
\f0\b the habitation of God
\f2\b0  in Christ by the Spirit.\
And this \'97 precisely this \'97 is what Part F will now unfold: that 
\f0\b we, the elect, have become the dwelling place of the Father in His Son by His Spirit
\f2\b0  \'97 drawn into the very Father-Son union that has existed from eternity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 READY FOR PART F\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We now have every piece in place:\
- 
\f0\b The Father is Eternal Spirit
\f2\b0  (Part E).\
- 
\f0\b The Father's Spirit indwelt the Son fully
\f2\b0  (John 14:10; Acts 10:38).\
- 
\f0\b The Son was glorified, received the Spirit from the Father, and poured it forth
\f2\b0  (Acts 2:33).\
- 
\f0\b The Spirit now indwells the elect permanently \'97 sealing them unto the day of redemption
\f2\b0  (Eph 1:13-14; 4:30; Rom 8:9-11).\
- 
\f0\b The OT pattern (Spirit upon) has given way to the NT pattern (Spirit within), made possible by the Son's completed work and irrevocable per the Father's promise
\f2\b0  (Rom 11:29).\
The stage is fully set. 
\f0\b Shall we now proceed to Part F \'97 The Indwelling: That We Should Be the Habitation of God in Christ
\f2\b0  \'97 beginning with 
\f0\b John 14:16-23 (Jesus' promise of the Father and Son making Their abode with us)
\f2\b0  and moving to 
\f0\b John 17:20-26 (the High Priestly Prayer for our oneness in Them)
\f2\b0 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 F.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We now arrive at 
\f0\b Part F \'97 The Indwelling: That We Should Be the Habitation of God in Christ.
\f2\b0  And we begin where Jesus Himself laid the foundation \'97 in the 
\f0\b Upper Room Discourse
\f2\b0  on the night of His betrayal, where He prepares His disciples for everything that was about to unfold.\
This is sacred ground. We will proceed slowly and reverently, per our refined modus operandi.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b JOHN 14:16-23 \'97 THE FATHER AND SON MAKING THEIR ABODE WITH US
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Context\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Jesus is in the Upper Room, hours before His arrest. He has just told the disciples He is going to prepare a place for them (14:1-6) and that He is the Way, the Truth, and the Life. He has told Philip that 
\f1\i "He that hath seen Me hath seen the Father"
\f2\i0  (14:9 \'97 which we already examined under Part E). He has promised that those who believe in Him will do greater works because He goes to the Father (14:12). And He has invited them to ask anything in His Name (14:13-14).\
Now He turns to the deepest disclosure: 
\f0\b what will happen after He is glorified \'97 how the Father and the Son will come to dwell in His disciples.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 14:16-17 \'97 THE OTHER PARACLETE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "And I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you forever, Even the Spirit of truth, whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, neither knoweth him: but ye know him: for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Clause-by-clause examination\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1) \uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u969  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u961 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "And I will ask the Father."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b The pattern is preserved.
\f2\b0  The Son 
\f0\b asks
\f2\b0 ; the Father 
\f0\b gives
\f2\b0 . Even at the climax of His ministry, the Son does not give the Spirit unilaterally \'97 He 
\f0\b asks
\f2\b0  the Father, and the Father 
\f0\b sends
\f2\b0 . This is consistent with everything we have established:\
- The Father is the 
\f0\b Source
\f2\b0  (1 Cor 8:6).\
- The Son is the 
\f0\b One who asks and receives
\f2\b0  (Ps 2:8; John 11:42).\
- The Father 
\f0\b gives
\f2\b0  in response to the Son's asking.\
This is also consistent with Acts 2:33 \'97 
\f1\i "having received from the Father the promise of the Holy Spirit, He poured forth..."
\f2\i0  The Father gives; the Son receives; the Son dispenses. 
\f0\b The chain is unbroken from the Father, through the Son, to the believer.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (2) \uc0\u7940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u961 \u940 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u948 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He will give you another Paraclete."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b \uc0\u928 \u945 \u961 \u940 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  is a rich term. Its root is 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u941 \u969 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to call alongside,"
\f2\i0  
\f1\i "to summon to one's aid,"
\f2\i0  
\f1\i "to comfort,"
\f2\i0  
\f1\i "to encourage,"
\f2\i0  
\f1\i "to advocate for."
\f2\i0  The 
\f0\b Paraclete
\f2\b0  is therefore:\
- One called alongside to help.\
- A comforter.\
- An advocate.\
- A counselor.\
The Geneva translates 
\f1\i "Comforter"
\f2\i0  \'97 capturing the consoling, strengthening dimension.\

\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "another"
\f2\i0  \'97 is critical. In Greek, 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  typically means 
\f1\i "another of the same kind"
\f2\i0  (as distinct from 
\f0\b \uc0\u7957 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0 , 
\f1\i "another of a different kind"
\f2\i0 ). Jesus is saying: 
\f0\b another Paraclete of the same kind as I am.
\f2\b0  This implies that 
\f0\b Jesus Himself has been functioning as a Paraclete to the disciples
\f2\b0  during His earthly ministry. He has been their Comforter, Advocate, Counselor. And now, when He goes, 
\f0\b another of the same kind
\f2\b0  will come.\
This is profoundly important for our study. The Paraclete who comes is not a totally different reality from Jesus' own presence \'97 He is 
\f0\b of the same character, same purpose, same indwelling presence.
\f2\b0  This is why John can later say that Christ is 
\f1\i in
\f2\i0  the believer (Gal 2:20; Col 1:27) \'97 because the Spirit who comes is the Spirit of the Father, which is also identified as the Spirit of the Son (Rom 8:9-10; Gal 4:6).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (3) \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u956 \u949 \u952 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8086  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "that He may be with you forever."
\f2\i0 \
We already examined this in the previous discussion \'97 
\f0\b forever.
\f2\b0  Not for a season, not for a task, not until the next sin \'97 but 
\f0\b forever
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 
\f2\b0 . This is the radical permanence of the New Covenant indwelling. The OT pattern of temporary visitation has given way to the eternal abiding presence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (4) \uc0\u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Spirit of Truth."
\f2\i0 \
This is the Paraclete's title. Why 
\f0\b "of Truth"
\f2\b0 ?\
- Because 
\f0\b the Father is Truth
\f2\b0  in His essential being.\
- Because 
\f0\b the Son is Truth
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I am the Way, the Truth, and the Life"
\f2\i0  (John 14:6).\
- Because the Spirit 
\f0\b reveals truth
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He will guide you into all truth"
\f2\i0  (John 16:13).\
- Because the Spirit 
\f0\b opposes the spirit of error
\f2\b0  (1 John 4:6).\
The Spirit of Truth is the Father's own essential Spirit, who knows the Father perfectly (1 Cor 2:10-11) and reveals what is true.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (5) \uc0\u8003  \u8001  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u959 \u8016  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u955 \u945 \u946 \u949 \u8150 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "whom the world cannot receive."
\f2\i0 \
This is a crucial point. 
\f0\b The world cannot receive the Spirit.
\f2\b0  Why?\
- The world does not believe in the Son (John 16:9).\
- The world has no organ to perceive the things of the Spirit (1 Cor 2:14).\
- The Spirit is given only to those who are joined to the Son by faith.\
This shows that the indwelling Spirit is 
\f0\b not a universal gift
\f2\b0  to all humanity \'97 it is the 
\f0\b specific possession of the elect
\f2\b0  who believe in the Son. The Spirit's indwelling is bound up with union with Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (6) \uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u959 \u8016  \u952 \u949 \u969 \u961 \u949 \u8150  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056  \u959 \u8016 \u948 \u8050  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "because it neither sees Him nor knows Him."
\f2\i0 \
The world cannot see Him (because the Spirit is invisible \'97 as Spirit, per Part E) and cannot know Him (because spiritual knowing requires spiritual indwelling).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (7) \uc0\u8017 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "You know Him, for He dwells with you, and shall be in you."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b This is the pivot of the entire discourse.
\f2\b0  Jesus distinguishes precisely:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 present tense \'97 
\f1\i "He 
\f3\b dwells with
\f1\b0  you."
\f2\i0  Right now, in this moment, the Spirit is 
\f0\b with
\f2\b0  them \'97 because He is in Jesus, who is with them. The Father's Spirit indwells the Son fully (John 14:10; Acts 10:38), and the Son is present with the disciples \'97 so the Spirit is 
\f1\i with
\f2\i0  them through Jesus' presence.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 future tense \'97 
\f1\i "He shall be 
\f3\b in
\f1\b0  you."
\f2\i0  After Jesus' glorification and the giving of the Spirit, 
\f0\b He will be in them
\f2\b0  \'97 internally indwelling.\

\f0\b This is Jesus' own announcement of the shift you identified.
\f2\b0  From OT-style "with/upon" to NT-style "within" \'97 and it happens at His glorification. The Spirit's location changes from "in the Son who is with us" to "in us, because the Son has given us His own Spirit through the Father."\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 14:18 \'97 I WILL COME TO YOU\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "I will not leave you fatherless: but I will come to you."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of decisive importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Jesus says: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u961 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "
\f3\b I
\f1\b0  am coming to you."
\f2\i0 \
But wait \'97 He has just said the 
\f1\i Paraclete
\f2\i0  will come. Now He says 
\f0\b He Himself
\f2\b0  will come. Are these two comings, or one?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The answer establishes a foundational truth:
\f2\b0  
\f0\b They are one coming.
\f2\b0  When the Spirit comes, 
\f0\b Jesus Himself comes.
\f2\b0  The Spirit's coming is Jesus' coming \'97 because the Spirit He sends is His own Spirit (the Father's Spirit, which fully indwelt Him and which He now pours forth).\
This is the basis for:\
- 
\f0\b 2 Corinthians 3:17
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Now the Lord is that Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Romans 8:9-10
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Spirit of God"
\f2\i0  and 
\f1\i "Spirit of Christ"
\f2\i0  and 
\f1\i "Christ in you"
\f2\i0  used interchangeably.\
- 
\f0\b Galatians 2:20
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Christ liveth in me."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Colossians 1:27
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Christ in you, the hope of glory."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b When the Spirit indwells, Christ indwells. When Christ indwells, the Father indwells (because the Father is in Christ). The mutual indwelling of the Father and Son is now extended to the believer through the Spirit.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 A Note on 
\f3\i "Fatherless / Orphans"
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u8000 \u961 \u966 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u973 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "orphans, fatherless."
\f2\i0  Jesus' departure would normally leave the disciples bereft, like orphans without a parent. But He promises: 
\f0\b He will not leave them so.
\f2\b0  He will come back to them \'97 through the Spirit who unites them to Himself and to the Father.\
This is the 
\f0\b Father-heart of Jesus' promise.
\f2\b0  He has been Father to them (Mark 10:24 \'97 
\f1\i "Children..."
\f2\i0 ), and He will not abandon them. They will not be orphans. They will have the Father \'97 through Him, by the Spirit.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 14:19-20 \'97 THE LIVING SON AND OUR ETERNAL UNION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Yet a little while, and the world shall see me no more, but ye shall see me: because I live, ye shall live also. At that day shall ye know that I am in my Father, and you in me, and I in you."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of supreme importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u950 \u8182  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8017 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u950 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u949 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Because I live, you shall live also."
\f2\i0 \
The Son's resurrection life becomes the source of the believer's life. 
\f0\b He lives
\f2\b0  \'97 and so 
\f0\b we shall live
\f2\b0 . Our life is derivative of His. This is the doctrinal basis of:\
- 
\f0\b Romans 6:4-5
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "as Christ was raised up from the dead..., even so we also should walk in newness of life... we shall be also in the likeness of his resurrection."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Colossians 3:3-4
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "your life is hid with Christ in God. When Christ, who is our life, shall appear..."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b 1 John 5:11-12
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "this is the record, that God hath given to us eternal life, and this life is in his Son."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b The Son's life is our life.
\f2\b0  Not separate; ours flows from His.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u954 \u949 \u943 \u957 \u8131  \u964 \u8135  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u8115  \u947 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "In that day you shall know..."
\f2\i0 \
What day? 
\f0\b The day of the Spirit's coming
\f2\b0  \'97 Pentecost forward. 
\f0\b Then
\f2\b0  they will know what they cannot know now.\
What will they know? 
\f0\b The triple indwelling pattern:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u943  \u956 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I am in My Father."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8017 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u943 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "You are in Me."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "and I am in you."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b This is the foundational disclosure.
\f2\b0  Let me draw it out:\

