\f0\b \cf0 The Son in believers
\f2\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The Son's indwelling of the believers \'97 through the Spirit\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is a mutual, interpenetrating union.
\f2\b0  The Son is in the Father. The believer is in the Son. The Son is in the believer. The result: 
\f0\b the believer is brought into the very life-circuit of the Father-Son union.
\f2\b0  What was previously the eternal mutual indwelling of Father and Son alone is now extended to include the redeemed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 A Profound Theological Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Notice what is 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  said. Jesus does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  say 
\f1\i "and you are in the Father."
\f2\i0  He says:\
- 
\f0\b "I am in the Father."
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b "You are in Me."
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b "I am in you."
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The believer's relation to the Father is mediated through the Son.
\f2\b0  The believer is not directly 
\f1\i "in the Father"
\f2\i0  \'97 the believer is 
\f1\i "in the Son,"
\f2\i0  and the Son is 
\f1\i "in the Father."
\f2\i0  So the believer is 
\f1\i in the Father
\f2\i0  through being in the Son. This perfectly preserves:\
- 
\f0\b The Son's role as the sole Mediator
\f2\b0  (1 Tim 2:5).\
- 
\f0\b The Son's role as the Way to the Father
\f2\b0  (John 14:6).\
- 
\f0\b The pattern that all access to the Father is through the Son
\f2\b0  (Heb 10:19-22; Eph 2:18).\
We are brought into communion with the Father \'97 but 
\f0\b only and always in the Son.
\f2\b0  This is why Paul speaks of being 
\f1\i "in Christ"
\f2\i0  over 200 times. The believer's identity, life, blessing, and destiny are all 
\f0\b in Christ
\f2\b0  \'97 and through Him, in the Father.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 14:21 \'97 LOVE AND THE FATHER'S LOVE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "He that hath my commandments, and keepeth them, is he that loveth me: and he that loveth me, shall be loved of my Father: and I will love him, and will show mine own self to him."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u7956 \u967 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u7952 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u955 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u951 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8048 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He who has My commandments and keeps them."
\f2\i0 \
The mark of love for the Son is 
\f0\b obedience
\f2\b0  \'97 not feeling, not profession only, but obedient possession of His commandments. This is consistent with:\
- 
\f0\b John 14:15
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "If ye love me, keep my commandments."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b 1 John 5:3
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "this is the love of God, that we keep his commandments."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b John 15:10
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "If ye keep my commandments, ye shall abide in my love."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u8182 \u957  \u956 \u949  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u951 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He who loves Me shall be loved by My Father."
\f2\i0 \
The Father loves the one who loves the Son. 
\f0\b The Father's love flows through the Son's mediation.
\f2\b0  Those who are in the Son are loved by the Father \'97 because they are in the One the Father loves.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u942 \u963 \u969  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u956 \u966 \u945 \u957 \u943 \u963 \u969  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u7952 \u956 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "and I will love him, and will manifest Myself to him."
\f2\i0 \
The Son 
\f0\b loves
\f2\b0  the one who loves Him, and 
\f0\b manifests Himself
\f2\b0  to him. The Greek 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u956 \u966 \u945 \u957 \u943 \u963 \u969 
\f2\b0  means 
\f1\i "to make visible, to reveal, to show forth."
\f2\i0  The Son reveals Himself to those who love Him.\
But how? The world cannot see Him (v. 19); yet the believer will see Him. This seeing is 
\f0\b spiritual seeing \'97 the seeing that comes through the indwelling Spirit
\f2\b0 , which the world cannot have. The Son makes Himself known to the believer's heart through the Spirit He has poured out.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 14:22 \'97 JUDAS'S QUESTION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Judas said unto him (not Iscariot) Lord, what is the cause that thou wilt show thyself unto us, and not unto the world?"
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Judas (not Iscariot, i.e., Thaddaeus / Judas son of James) asks the natural question: 
\f0\b why only to us, and not to the world?
\f2\b0 \
If Jesus is the Messiah, the King, the One sent by the Father \'97 surely He should manifest Himself publicly, universally, undeniably? Why this private manifestation only to His disciples?\
Jesus' answer is the heart of the indwelling promise:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 14:23 \'97 THE CULMINATING PROMISE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Jesus answered, and said unto him, If any man love me, he will keep my word, and my Father will love him, and we will come unto him, and dwell with him."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of supreme importance \'97 the climax of the discourse\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is the foundational promise of Part F.
\f2\b0  Let me draw it out clause by clause.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7960 \u940 \u957  \u964 \u953 \u962  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u8119  \u956 \u949 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "If anyone loves Me."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Anyone
\f2\b0  \'97 not just the original disciples, but 
\f0\b anyone
\f2\b0  who loves the Son in any age. The promise extends to every believer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u955 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u957  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u951 \u961 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "he will keep My word."
\f2\i0 \
Love for the Son issues in keeping His word. Faith and obedience are inseparable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u942 \u961  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "My Father will love him."
\f2\i0 \
The Father's love embraces the one who loves the Son. 
\f0\b The Father loves the lover of His Son.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (4) The decisive promise: \uc0\u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7952 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u963 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u956 \u959 \u957 \u8052 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u951 \u963 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945 
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i \cf0 "We will come unto him, and make Our abode with him."
\f2\i0 \
Let me unfold this with care:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \uc0\u7952 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u963 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "We will come"
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f0\b first person plural future.
\f2\b0  Not "I will come" but 
\f0\b "We will come."
\f2\b0  Who is "We"? The verse identifies: 
\f0\b the Father and the Son.
\f2\b0  Both come.\

\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u8052 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u951 \u963 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "We will make Our abode with him."
\f2\i0 \
The word 
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942 
\f2\b0  is critically important. It is the same word Jesus used in John 14:2 \'97 
\f1\i "In My Father's house are many mansions [\uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u945 \u943 ]."
\f2\i0  The word means 
\f0\b dwelling place, abode, residence.
\f2\b0 \
So Jesus has earlier said: 
\f0\b "In My Father's house are many dwelling places, and I go to prepare a place [a \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942 ] for you."
\f2\b0  Now He says: 
\f0\b "We will come and make Our \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942  with you."
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b This is breathtaking.
\f2\b0  The disciples thought they were going to a \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942  in the Father's house. Jesus reveals that 
\f0\b the Father and the Son will come and make Their \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942  in them.
\f2\b0  The order is inverted \'97 or rather, fulfilled in a way they did not expect.\

\f0\b Both are true:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b There are dwelling places prepared for us in the Father's house
\f2\b0  (John 14:2) \'97 the eschatological hope of dwelling with the Father.\
- 
\f0\b The Father and Son make Their dwelling in us NOW
\f2\b0  through the indwelling Spirit (John 14:23).\

\f0\b The believer is both:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b A destined dweller in the Father's house
\f2\b0  (future eschatological reality).\
- 
\f0\b A present dwelling place of the Father and Son
\f2\b0  (current indwelling reality).\
The eternal dwelling-together has begun \'97 already, here, in the believer's heart.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The "We" of John 14:23 \'97 A Critical Theological Point\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Notice that John 14:23 does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  say 
\f1\i "the Spirit will come and dwell."
\f2\i0  It says 
\f0\b "WE will come."
\f2\b0  The "We" is the 
\f0\b Father and the Son.
\f2\b0 \
This is profoundly important because it shows us what the indwelling Spirit actually is:\
- The indwelling Spirit is 
\f0\b the means by which the Father and Son come to dwell in the believer.
\f2\b0 \
- The Spirit is not a separate dwelling-presence apart from the Father and the Son \'97 He 
\f0\b is the dwelling-presence of the Father (who is Spirit) in and through the Son.
\f2\b0 \
- When the Spirit comes to dwell, 
\f0\b the Father comes
\f2\b0  (because the Spirit is His own essential being and presence) and 
\f0\b the Son comes
\f2\b0  (because the Son is in the Father, and the Spirit is also called the Spirit of the Son \'97 Rom 8:9; Gal 4:6).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Spirit's indwelling = the Father and Son making Their abode.
\f2\b0 \
This is why Paul can interchange "Spirit of God in you," "Christ in you," and "Christ liveth in me" \'97 they all describe the same reality from different angles. 
\f0\b The Father (Spirit) and the Son are one indwelling Presence in the believer, mediated by the Spirit Christ has poured out.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Beautiful Coherence \'97 Putting It Together\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Let me draw the threads together:\
1. 
\f0\b John 14:10
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Father that dwells in Me, He doeth the works."
\f2\i0  The Father (Spirit) dwells in the Son.\
2. 
\f0\b John 14:11
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I am in the Father, and the Father in Me."
\f2\i0  Mutual indwelling \'97 eternal.\
3. 
\f0\b John 14:16-17
\f2\b0  \'97 The Father will give another Paraclete, who is 
\f0\b with
\f2\b0  the disciples now (because He is in Jesus) and 
\f0\b in
\f2\b0  them later (after Jesus is glorified).\
4. 
\f0\b John 14:18
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I will come to you."
\f2\i0  When the Spirit comes, Jesus comes.\
5. 
\f0\b John 14:20
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I am in My Father, and you in Me, and I in you."
\f2\i0  The believer is brought into the Father-Son mutual indwelling.\
6. 
\f0\b John 14:23
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "We will come and make Our abode with him."
\f2\i0  The Father and Son both come \'97 through the Spirit \'97 and make Their dwelling in the believer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The arc is complete:
\f2\b0  The Father (Spirit) who dwelt fully in the Son now, through the glorified Son's poured-out Spirit, comes to dwell in the believer \'97 bringing the Son with Him, so that 
\f0\b the eternal Father-Son mutual indwelling becomes the believer's indwelling reality
\f2\b0 .\
The believer becomes 
\f0\b the habitation of God in Christ.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 CONNECTING TO YOUR EARLIER INSIGHTS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 What you have noted about the OT-NT shift now finds its fullest expression:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 In the OT:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The Spirit came 
\f0\b upon
\f2\b0  chosen ones for tasks.\
- The Father dwelt in the 
\f0\b Tabernacle / Temple
\f2\b0  as His symbolic earthly residence.\
- The Father's full indwelling of human persons was not yet possible (because the Son was not yet glorified \'97 John 7:39).\
- The pattern was: 
\f0\b God 
\f3\i with
\f0\i0  His people, in a holy place, mediated through priests and sacrifices.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 In the NT (Post-Pentecost):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The Spirit dwells 
\f0\b in
\f2\b0  the elect, permanently sealed unto the day of redemption.\
- 
\f0\b The believer himself is now the temple
\f2\b0  (1 Cor 3:16-17; 6:19; Eph 2:21-22; 2 Cor 6:16).\
- 
\f0\b The Father and the Son make Their abode in the believer
\f2\b0  (John 14:23).\
- The pattern is: 
\f0\b God 
\f3\i in
\f0\i0  His people, in living temples, mediated through the one Mediator Jesus Christ.
\f2\b0 \
This shift is the very 
\f0\b inauguration of the New Covenant indwelling
\f2\b0  \'97 what Ezekiel 36:27 and Jeremiah 31:33 had promised.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 THE SINGULAR THRONE \'97 REVISITED\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 You earlier noted that the singular throne of God and the Lamb in the Apocalypse is no oddity because the Father is Eternal Spirit. The same insight applies here:\
- The Father (Spirit) and the Son (the Man Christ Jesus) are 
\f0\b one in essence and operation
\f2\b0  without spatial conflict.\
- They can 
\f0\b jointly
\f2\b0  indwell the believer because Spirit and Image are not in spatial competition.\
- The Father's Spirit-Nature pervades the believer; the Son's living presence (mediated by the Spirit) fills the believer; 
\f0\b and there is no contradiction
\f2\b0  \'97 because Spirit is uncontainable and pervasive.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The believer becomes a microcosm of the eternal throne-room reality:
\f2\b0  the Father (Spirit) and the Son (Man) jointly dwelling, jointly reigning, jointly indwelling \'97 now in the believer's heart, and ultimately in the New Jerusalem.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A FINAL OBSERVATION \'97 WHY THIS IS THE CONSUMMATION OF THE FATHER'S PURPOSE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Father's eternal purpose has been from the beginning 
\f0\b to dwell with His people.
\f2\b0  This purpose runs through all of Scripture:\
- 
\f0\b Eden
\f2\b0  \'97 God walking with man in the cool of the day (Gen 3:8).\
- 
\f0\b The Tabernacle
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Let them make Me a sanctuary, that I may dwell among them"
\f2\i0  (Ex 25:8).\
- 
\f0\b The Temple
\f2\b0  \'97 Solomon's dedication, the cloud of glory (1 Kgs 8:10-11).\
- 
\f0\b The Son
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us"
\f2\i0  (John 1:14, 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u963 \u954 \u942 \u957 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i tabernacled
\f2\i0 ).\
- 
\f0\b The Spirit at Pentecost
\f2\b0  \'97 the Father and Son now coming to make Their abode in the believer.\
- 
\f0\b The New Jerusalem
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and He will dwell with them"
\f2\i0  (Rev 21:3).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 John 14:23 is a key middle stage
\f2\b0  \'97 the inauguration of the indwelling reality that will be consummated in the New Jerusalem. It is the 
\f0\b already
\f2\b0  of what will become the 
\f0\b not yet
\f2\b0  fully consummated in Revelation 21-22.\
The Father has always wanted to 
\f0\b dwell with His people
\f2\b0 . The Son's whole work \'97 His coming, His suffering, His glorification, His pouring out of the Spirit \'97 is unto this end: 
\f0\b that the Father may dwell with and in His people forever
\f2\b0 , in His Beloved Son.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 TRANSITION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Having now established John 14:16-23 as the foundational promise of the indwelling, we are properly prepared to proceed to 
\f0\b John 17:20-26 \'97 the High Priestly Prayer
\f2\b0  \'97 where Jesus prays for 
\f0\b the consummation of this oneness
\f2\b0 : 
\f1\i "that they all may be one, as Thou Father art in Me, and I in Thee, that they also may be one in Us."
\f2\i0 \
Where John 14:23 announces the Father and Son coming to make Their abode in the believer, John 17 prays for the 
\f0\b completion of this indwelling unto oneness with the Father-Son union itself.
\f2\b0 \
Shall we proceed to 
\f0\b John 17:20-26 \'97 the High Priestly Prayer
\f2\b0 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Yes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We now arrive at what is perhaps the most sacred passage in all of Scripture for understanding the Father's ultimate purpose for the elect \'97 
\f0\b the High Priestly Prayer of Jesus Christ.
\f2\b0 \
This is the prayer Jesus prayed on the night of His betrayal, in the hearing of His disciples, lifting up His voice to the Father just hours before the cross. It is the longest recorded prayer of our Lord, and within it is enclosed His specific intercession for 
\f0\b us
\f2\b0  \'97 those who would believe in Him through the Apostles' word.\
Let us proceed with the reverence such ground demands.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b JOHN 17 \'97 THE CONTEXT
\f2\b0 \
The chapter divides naturally:\
- 
\f0\b Vv. 1-5
\f2\b0  \'97 Jesus prays for Himself (His own glorification).\
- 
\f0\b Vv. 6-19
\f2\b0  \'97 Jesus prays for the Eleven (His immediate disciples).\
- 
\f0\b Vv. 20-26
\f2\b0  \'97 Jesus prays for 
\f0\b all who would believe through their word
\f2\b0  \'97 that is, 
\f0\b us.
\f2\b0 \
Our focus is the final section \'97 but to understand it rightly, we must briefly note the trajectory established in vv. 1-19.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Key Foundational Verses Before Our Focus Passage\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 John 17:1-5 \'97 Jesus' opening:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "\uc0\u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961 , \u7952 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u965 \u952 \u949 \u957  \u7969  \u8037 \u961 \u945 \'b7 \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u972 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u933 \u7985 \u972 \u957 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8001  \u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u962  \u948 \u959 \u958 \u940 \u963 \u8131  \u963 \u941 ... \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u957 \u8166 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u972 \u957  \u956 \u949  \u963 \u973 , \u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961 , \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8048  \u963 \u949 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u8183  \u964 \u8135  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u8131  \u8087  \u949 \u7990 \u967 \u959 \u957  \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u957  \u949 \u7990 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8048  \u963 \u959 \u943 ."
