\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 17:20 \'97 The Scope Widens to Include Us\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "I pray not for these alone, but for them also which shall believe in me, through their word,"
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of supreme weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u927 \u8016  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u948 \u8050  \u7952 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u8182  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I do not ask concerning these only."
\f2\i0  Jesus' prayer now widens beyond the eleven physically present with Him.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u965 \u972 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u955 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u965  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7952 \u956 \u941 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "of those who believe in Me through their word."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b This is us.
\f2\b0  Every believer from Pentecost forward who has come to faith 
\f0\b through the apostolic word
\f2\b0  \'97 that is, the Gospel as proclaimed by the Apostles and preserved in their writings (the New Testament) \'97 is included in this prayer. The chain is:\
- The Father sends the Son (v. 3).\
- The Son trains and sends the Apostles (vv. 6-19; cf. v. 18).\
- The Apostles proclaim the Word.\
- Believers come to faith through the apostolic word.\
- These believers are who Jesus prays for here.\

\f0\b Per maxim #1, this prayer is Jesus' own intercession for 
\f3\i every
\f0\i0  elect believer through the present age.
\f2\b0  This is the prayer of the great High Priest \'97 His ongoing intercession (Heb 7:25; Rom 8:34) \'97 recorded for us so we may know what He prays.\

\f0\b (3) The present participle \uc0\u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u965 \u972 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "those who are believing"
\f2\i0  \'97 is significant. The believing is not a one-time historical event but the continuing posture of those who have received the Apostles' testimony.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 17:21 \'97 THE CENTRAL PETITION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "That they all may be one, as thou, O Father, art in me, and I in thee: even that they may be also one in us, that the world may believe that thou hast sent me."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Let us examine this verse with the care it demands.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is 
\f0\b the central petition of the entire prayer
\f2\b0 , and it contains four critical clauses:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 #### 
\f0\b Clause 1: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u7955 \u957  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \'97 
\f3\i "that they all may be one"
\f2\i0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \uc0\u7955 \u957  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "may be one."
\f2\i0  The verb is 
\f0\b subjunctive
\f2\b0  (purpose), and the predicate 
\f0\b \uc0\u7957 \u957 
\f2\b0  is neuter \'97 
\f1\i "one [thing]."
\f2\i0  Not numerically one (as in one person), but 
\f0\b unified in being / one in essential reality.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b The petition:
\f2\b0  That all believers from Pentecost forward may be 
\f0\b one
\f2\b0 . This is not asking for organizational unity, denominational uniformity, or political consolidation. This is a far deeper unity \'97 defined by the next clause.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 #### 
\f0\b Clause 2: \uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u963 \u973 , \u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961 , \u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8054  \u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u943  \'97 
\f3\i "even as Thou, Father, art in Me, and I in Thee"
\f2\i0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The model.
\f2\b0  The oneness Jesus prays for is patterned after 
\f0\b the mutual indwelling of the Father and the Son.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u974 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "even as / according as / in the same manner as."
\f2\i0  The believers' oneness is to be 
\f0\b of the same character
\f2\b0  as the Father-Son oneness \'97 though, as we shall see, not identical in essence.\

\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u973 , \u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961 , \u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8054 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Thou, Father, in Me."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u943 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "and I in Thee."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Mutual indwelling.
\f2\b0  The Father is in the Son; the Son is in the Father. This is the eternal reality we established in Part E \'97 the Father (Spirit) indwells the Son (Image), and the Son is in the Father (in the Father's Spirit-presence).\

\f0\b The prototype is established.
\f2\b0  The Father-Son union is the model for the believers' union.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 #### 
\f0\b Clause 3: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \'97 
\f3\i "that they also may be in Us"
\f2\i0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Here is the breathtaking petition.
\f2\b0  The Greek is: 
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8054 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "they also"
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "in Us"
\f2\i0  \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "may be."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b "In Us."
\f2\b0  Believers are to be 
\f0\b in the Father and in the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 drawn into the Father-Son mutual indwelling.\
This is staggering, and we must handle it with great care. Let me draw it out precisely:\

\f0\b The pattern of John 14:20 was:
\f2\b0 \
- I am in the Father.\
- You are in Me.\
- I am in you.\

\f0\b The pattern of John 17:21 is:
\f2\b0 \
- The Father is in Me; I am in the Father (mutual indwelling).\
- That 
\f0\b they may be in Us
\f2\b0  \'97 drawn into this mutual indwelling.\

\f0\b The believer is not directly "in the Father" apart from the Son.
\f2\b0  Note carefully: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "in Us."
\f2\i0  The "Us" is the Father and the Son together. The believer is brought into the joint reality of the Father-Son union \'97 
\f0\b through being in the Son who is in the Father.
\f2\b0 \
This perfectly preserves what we established in our earlier examination of John 14:20:\
- 
\f0\b The believer's relation to the Father is mediated through the Son.
\f2\b0 \
- The believer is 
\f1\i in the Son
\f2\i0 ; the Son is 
\f1\i in the Father
\f2\i0 ; therefore the believer is brought 
\f1\i into the Father-Son union
\f2\i0 .\
- The Son remains the sole Mediator (1 Tim 2:5).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 #### 
\f0\b Clause 4: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8001  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u8131  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u963 \u973  \u956 \u949  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u945 \u962  \'97 
\f3\i "that the world may believe that Thou hast sent Me"
\f2\i0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The purpose of the oneness is missional.
\f2\b0  The world's faith in the Father's sending of the Son depends on 
\f0\b the visible oneness of His people.
\f2\b0  When the world sees believers genuinely united in the Father-Son reality, the world is given evidence that Jesus was indeed sent from God.\
This is a profound truth: 
\f0\b our oneness is the Father's evidence to the world.
\f2\b0  The disunity of professing Christians has been a great hindrance to the Gospel's progress.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 JOHN 17:22 \'97 THE GLORY GIVEN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "And the glory that thou gavest me, I have given them, that they may be one, as we are one,"
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u7971 \u957  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u953  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the glory which Thou hast given Me, I have given them."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Trace the chain:
\f2\b0 \
- The Father 
\f0\b gave
\f2\b0  glory to the Son (\uc0\u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \'97 perfect tense \'97 completed past with continuing effect).\
- The Son 
\f0\b gave
\f2\b0  that same glory to the believers (\uc0\u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u945  \'97 perfect tense \'97 completed past with continuing effect).\

\f0\b Both verbs are in the perfect tense
\f2\b0  \'97 denoting an action accomplished with abiding result. The glory has been 
\f0\b given
\f2\b0 , and 
\f0\b continues to belong
\f2\b0  to the recipients.\

\f0\b What glory is this?
\f2\b0  Not the glory of inherent deity (which the Father has alone), but 
\f0\b the glory the Father gave the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 the glory of being the Beloved Son, of being commissioned, of being indwelt by the Father's Spirit, of being the perfect Image of the invisible God. This is the glory 
\f0\b received
\f2\b0  by the Son from the Father \'97 and this is the glory the Son passes on to the elect.\

\f0\b The elect receive glory by participation in the Son's glory.
\f2\b0  Not the original, unshared glory of the Father (1 Tim 1:17 \'97 
\f1\i "glory forever and ever"
\f2\i0  \'97 uniquely His); but the 
\f0\b derived, given glory
\f2\b0  that the Son received and now shares with His people.\
This is consistent with:\
- 
\f0\b Romans 8:17
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "if so be that we suffer with him, that we may be also glorified together."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Romans 8:30
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "whom he justified, them he also glorified."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b 2 Corinthians 3:18
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "we all... beholding... the glory of the Lord, are changed into the same image from glory to glory."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Colossians 3:4
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "when Christ, who is our life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with him in glory."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b 2 Thessalonians 2:14
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to the obtaining of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b The Son's glory becomes the believer's glory
\f2\b0  \'97 given, not earned; received, not innate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (2)
\f2\b0  
