\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961  \u948 \u943 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u949 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Righteous Father."
\f2\i0  The address. The Father is 
\f0\b righteous
\f2\b0  \'97 meaning, what He does and how He distinguishes between the world (which has not known Him) and the disciples (who have known Him through the Son) is 
\f0\b just
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b right.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (2) The three-fold distinction:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b "The world has not known Thee."
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b "I have known Thee."
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b "These have known that Thou hast sent Me."
\f2\b0 \
The world's failure to know the Father is set against the Son's perfect knowledge of Him and the disciples' knowledge \'97 through the Son \'97 that the Father sent Him. The chain of knowing:\
- 
\f0\b The Son knows the Father directly
\f2\b0  (because He is the only-begotten in the Father's bosom \'97 John 1:18).\
- 
\f0\b The disciples know that the Father sent the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 and through this knowledge, they have access to the Father (because the Son is the Way \'97 John 14:6).\
- 
\f0\b The world does not know either
\f2\b0  \'97 having no organ of spiritual perception.\
