\f0\b \cf0 (4) The Final, Climactic Purpose: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u7969  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951  \u7971 \u957  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u8086  \u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i \cf0 "that the love wherewith Thou hast loved Me may be in them, and I in them."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 This is the crowning petition.
\f2\b0  Let me unfold it slowly.\

\f0\b \uc0\u7969  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951  \u7971 \u957  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u949 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the love with which Thou hast loved Me."
\f2\i0  This is the 
\f0\b eternal love of the Father for the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 the love we noted in v. 24 that pre-dates creation. The same love.\

\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u8086 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "may be in them."
\f2\i0  That this very love \'97 the Father's love for the Son \'97 may 
\f0\b be in
\f2\b0  the believers.\

\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "and I in them."
\f2\i0  And the Son Himself in them.\

\f0\b Together:
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The Father's eternal love for the Son, AND the Son Himself, in the believers.
\f2\b0 \
Stop and consider what this means. The Father has loved the Son with eternal, undivided, perfect love from before the foundation of the world. 
\f0\b That very love
\f2\b0  is now poured into the believer. And the 
\f0\b Son Himself
\f2\b0  \'97 the Beloved One \'97 is in the believer.\
This is the consummation of indwelling:\
- 
\f0\b The Father's love
\f2\b0  \'97 the love that has always been between Father and Son \'97 is now poured into us.\
- 
\f0\b The Son
\f2\b0  \'97 the Beloved \'97 is in us.\
- The two \'97 love and Lover \'97 together fill the believer.\
And how does this happen? 
\f0\b Through the indwelling Spirit
\f2\b0 , which is the Father's own essential being and presence, poured out through the Son (Acts 2:33).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
