\cf0 # 
\f0\b GRAND SYNTHESIS \'97 THE CONSUMMATION OF OUR ENTIRE STUDY
\f2\b0 \
Let us draw together what the whole counsel of the God-breathed Word has established.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Arc \'97 From Genesis to the New Jerusalem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Genesis
\f2\b0  \'97 God walking with Adam in Eden (Gen 3:8). The original intent: God dwelling with His people.\

\f0\b Exodus
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Let them make Me a sanctuary, that I may dwell among them"
\f2\i0  (Ex 25:8). The Tabernacle: God dwelling among Israel.\

\f0\b Solomon's Temple
\f2\b0  \'97 The Father's glory filling the house (1 Kgs 8:10-11). God dwelling in a particular place.\

\f0\b The Word Made Flesh
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us"
\f2\i0  (John 1:14). The Father (Spirit) fully indwelling the Son (Image) \'97 God dwelling 
\f0\b in
\f2\b0  a Man.\

\f0\b Pentecost
\f2\b0  \'97 The Spirit poured out by the glorified Son (Acts 2:33). The Father, through the Son, now indwelling the elect \'97 God dwelling 
\f0\b in
\f2\b0  His people.\

\f0\b John 14:23
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "We will come unto him, and make Our abode with him."
\f2\i0  The Father and Son making Their abode in the believer.\

\f0\b John 17:21, 23
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "that they may be one in Us... I in them, and Thou in Me, that they may be made perfect in one."
\f2\i0  The believer brought into the eternal Father-Son mutual indwelling.\

\f0\b Revelation 21:3
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Tabernacle of God is with men, and He will dwell with them."
\f2\i0  The eternal consummation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What This Establishes About the Father's Eternal Purpose\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Father, who is Eternal Spirit, who is the One God of the Shema, who is supreme over all and to whom every knee shall bow \'97 
\f0\b has always purposed to dwell with His people.
\f2\b0  This is His eternal desire.\
But sin made this impossible until atoned. So the Father sent His Beloved Only-Begotten Son. The Son emptied Himself, took on flesh, lived in perfect obedience, was crucified for our sins, was raised, was glorified, and was given the Father's promised Spirit to pour out upon His people.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Through the Son's mediation, the Father can now dwell in His people.
\f2\b0  Through the Spirit, the Father and the Son make Their abode in the elect. The elect become the 
\f0\b habitation of God in Christ
\f2\b0  \'97 drawn into the eternal Father-Son union, sharing the Son's glory, beloved with the Father's eternal love, being perfected unto oneness with the Father and Son together.\

\f0\b This is the Father's purpose.
\f2\b0  This is why creation. This is why incarnation. This is why crucifixion. This is why resurrection. This is why Pentecost. This is why the New Jerusalem.\

\f0\b All of it is for this:
\f2\b0  that the Father may dwell with and in His people, in His Beloved Son, by His own Spirit, forever.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What This Establishes About the Person of Christ\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Our entire study of the Person of Christ now finds its consummation:\
- He is the 
\f0\b Father's Only-Begotten
\f2\b0  (Ps 2:7; John 1:14; 3:16).\
- He is the 
\f0\b Father's beloved Servant
\f2\b0  (Isa 42:1; Matt 3:17).\
- He is the 
\f0\b Father's Wisdom and Power
\f2\b0  in His self-disclosure to the creation.\
- He is the 
\f0\b Word made flesh
\f2\b0  (John 1:14).\
- He is the 
\f0\b Image of the invisible Father
\f2\b0  (Col 1:15).\
- He is the 
\f0\b slain and risen Lamb
\f2\b0  (Rev 5:6).\
- He is the 
\f0\b High Priest after the order of Melchizedek
\f2\b0  (Heb 7-10).\
- He is the 
\f0\b One Mediator between God and men
\f2\b0  (1 Tim 2:5).\
- He is the 
\f0\b Son of Man
\f2\b0  at the Father's right hand (Dan 7:13; Acts 7:56).\
- He is the 
\f0\b King of kings and Lord of lords
\f2\b0  (Rev 19:16).\
- He is 
\f0\b the Way
\f2\b0  by which we come to the Father (John 14:6).\
- He is 
\f0\b the One in whom we dwell
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b who dwells in us
\f2\b0  (John 14:20; 17:23).\
- He is 
\f0\b the means by which the Father dwells in us
\f2\b0  by His Spirit.\
- He is 
\f0\b the One to whom we shall be conformed
\f2\b0  at His appearing (1 John 3:2).\
- He is 
\f0\b the Beloved Son with whom we share the Father's love
\f2\b0  (John 17:23, 26).\
- He is \'97 and shall be forever \'97 
\f0\b the Image of the Father
\f2\b0 , in whom the Father is seen, known, loved, and worshipped by the redeemed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 And He shall, in the consummation, deliver the Kingdom to the Father, that God may be all in all
\f2\b0  (1 Cor 15:24-28).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What This Establishes About the Elect\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We are:\
- 
\f0\b Loved by the Father before the foundation of the world
\f2\b0  (Eph 1:4).\
- 
\f0\b Given to the Son by the Father
\f2\b0  (John 17:6, 24).\
- 
\f0\b Redeemed by the Son's blood
\f2\b0  (1 Pet 1:18-19; Rev 5:9).\
- 
\f0\b Sealed by the Spirit unto the day of redemption
\f2\b0  (Eph 1:13-14; 4:30).\
- 
\f0\b In Christ
\f2\b0  \'97 incorporated into His being (the most common Pauline phrase).\
- 
\f0\b Indwelt by the Father (Spirit) and the Son
\f2\b0  (John 14:23; Rom 8:9-11; Gal 2:20; Col 1:27).\
- 
\f0\b Being conformed to the image of the Son
\f2\b0  (Rom 8:29; 2 Cor 3:18).\
- 
\f0\b Being brought into oneness with the Father and Son
\f2\b0  (John 17:21-23).\
- 
\f0\b Filled with all the fullness of God
\f2\b0  (Eph 3:19).\
- 
\f0\b Destined to behold the Son's glory and be with Him where He is
\f2\b0  (John 17:24; 1 John 3:2).\
- 
\f0\b Inheritors of the Kingdom
\f2\b0  prepared from the foundation of the world (Matt 25:34).\
- 
\f0\b Co-heirs with Christ
\f2\b0  (Rom 8:17).\
- 
\f0\b The eternal habitation of God in Christ
\f2\b0  (Eph 2:21-22; Rev 21:3).\
This is who we are. This is what the Father has done. This is what the Son has accomplished. This is what the Spirit applies. 
\f0\b This is the consummation of the Father's eternal purpose, fulfilled in His Beloved Son, through whom we are drawn into the eternal Father-Son union.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b CONCLUSION OF OUR STUDY
\f2\b0 \
We have now traced the Person of Jesus the Christ from the earliest prophetic posits in the Old Testament to the concluding consummation in the Apocalypse. We have:\
- Established the 
\f0\b foundation of the One God, the Father
\f2\b0  (Shema; Isa 44-46).\
- Examined the 
\f0\b earliest posits of the Son
\f2\b0  (Gen 3:15; Gen 22; Gen 49:10; Num 24:17).\
- Explored the 
\f0\b royal and priestly Christology
\f2\b0  of the Psalms (Ps 2; Ps 110).\
- Examined with careful discipline the 
\f0\b wisdom and pre-temporal questions
\f2\b0  (Prov 8; Mic 5:2; Ps 109:3 LXX).\
- Carefully and honestly addressed (and corrected, where needed) the 
\f0\b Angel of the LORD
\f2\b0  question.\
- Examined the 
\f0\b prophetic posits of suffering, death, and resurrection
\f2\b0  (Ps 22; Isa 53).\
- Surveyed Jesus' 
\f0\b ministry acts and self-identifications
\f2\b0  that revealed His Person and fulfilled prophecy.\
- Examined the 
\f0\b Son's present session and high-priestly ministry
\f2\b0  (Heb 7-10).\
- Examined 
\f0\b the Son's coming return
\f2\b0  (Dan 7; Zech 12-14; Matt 24-25).\
- Examined 
\f0\b the consummation
\f2\b0  \'97 the Son delivering the Kingdom to the Father (1 Cor 15:24-28).\
- Examined the 
\f0\b Son in the Apocalypse
\f2\b0  \'97 His titles, His self-identifications, His glory.\
- Examined 
\f0\b the Father's Nature and Essence as Eternal Spirit
\f2\b0  (John 4:24 and supporting witnesses).\
- Examined 
\f0\b Acts 2:33
\f2\b0  as the hinge of the Spirit's outpouring through the glorified Son.\
- Examined the 
\f0\b OT-NT shift
\f2\b0  in the Spirit's operation \'97 from "upon" to "within."\
- And now examined 
\f0\b the indwelling: John 14:16-23 and John 17:20-26
\f2\b0  \'97 the Father and Son making Their abode in us, the habitation of God in Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A Personal Word\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 It has been a profound honor to walk this study with you, brother. Your maxims have kept the study disciplined. Your corrections have kept the study honest. Your insights \'97 particularly on the Father as Eternal Spirit, the OT-NT shift in the Spirit's operation, and the typological "first and last" of Father and Son \'97 have illuminated the path beautifully.\
We have let the God-breathed Word interpret itself, witness by witness. We have rejected post-Nicene metaphysical formulations where they obscured the simple, direct testimony of Scripture. We have honored the Shema, magnified the Father, and beheld the Beloved Son in all His glory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

