\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 WHAT THIS ESTABLISHES \'97 THE ULTIMATE COHERENCE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The believer is identified with Christ 
\f0\b in every redemptive act of the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 past, present, and future. There is no facet of the Son's saving work in which we do not participate by virtue of being 
\f0\b in Him.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 This is not metaphor.
\f2\b0  Paul does not say 
\f1\i "as if we were crucified with Him."
\f2\i0  He says 
\f1\i "I have been crucified with Christ"
\f2\i0  \'97 perfect tense, real reality. Not a legal fiction, not a poetic figure, but the 
\f0\b actual reckoning of the Father
\f2\b0  that includes us in His Son's history and destiny.\

\f0\b The mechanism:
\f2\b0  The Father, who is Eternal Spirit, chose us in His Beloved Son before the foundation of the world. He so identified us with His Son that what the Son did, we did in Him. The Son's death is our death; His burial is our burial; His resurrection is our resurrection; His ascension is our ascension; His seating is our seating; His glory is our glory; His inheritance is our inheritance.\

\f0\b Therefore:
\f2\b0 \
- We do not need to add to His work. It is complete.\
- We do not need to fear condemnation. We are in Him who is acquitted.\
- We do not need to seek our own righteousness. We have His.\
- We do not need to seek our own glory. We are joint-heirs of His.\
- We do not need to fear death. We have already died with Him.\
- We do not need to fear judgment. We have already been justified in Him.\

\f0\b We are who He is \'97 not in essence, but in identification by the Father's reckoning and the Spirit's union.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 GALATIANS 2:20 \'97 REVISITED IN LIGHT OF THE WHOLE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Now we can hear Paul's testimony with full resonance:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i \cf0 "I have been crucified with Christ"
\f2\i0  \'97 co-crucified, established by Rom 6:6.\

\f1\i "It is no longer I who live"
\f2\i0  \'97 the old man is dead, new creation is the reality (2 Cor 5:17).\

\f1\i "But Christ lives in me"
\f2\i0  \'97 the indwelling of the Son, established by John 14:20, 23; Col 1:27.\

\f1\i "And the life which I now live in the flesh, I live by faith in the Son of God"
\f2\i0  \'97 by present faith we appropriate this identification daily.\

\f1\i "Who loved me and gave Himself for me"
\f2\i0  \'97 the personal, individual love of the Beloved Son for each elect believer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 This is not Paul alone. This is every believer.
\f2\b0  Every elect saint can say with Paul: 
\f1\i "I have been crucified with Christ; I no longer live; Christ lives in me; I live by faith of the Son of God who loved me and gave Himself for me."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b A CLOSING OBSERVATION
\f2\b0 \
Brother, what we have surveyed here is the 
\f0\b richest doctrinal treasure of the New Testament.
\f2\b0  The believer's identification in Christ is the basis of:\
- Our 
\f0\b security
\f2\b0  \'97 we are in Him who cannot be lost.\
- Our 
\f0\b standing
\f2\b0  \'97 we are accepted in the Beloved.\
- Our 
\f0\b sanctification
\f2\b0  \'97 we are being conformed to His image.\
- Our 
\f0\b service
\f2\b0  \'97 we live not for ourselves but for Him who loved us.\
- Our 
\f0\b suffering
\f2\b0  \'97 we share His cross, knowing it leads to His crown.\
- Our 
\f0\b hope
\f2\b0  \'97 we shall appear with Him in glory.\
Every fear, every doubt, every accusation of the enemy is answered in this single phrase: 
\f0\b "in Christ."
\f2\b0 \
We are 
\f0\b in Him
\f2\b0  \'97 and therefore everything the Father has decreed concerning the Son flows to us by identification. We are not aliens looking on; 
\f0\b we are members of His body, of His flesh, of His bones.
\f2\b0  We are not orphans hoping for adoption; 
\f0\b we are children of God, joint-heirs with Christ.
\f2\b0  We are not sinners hoping for mercy; 
\f0\b we are crucified with Christ, dead to sin, alive to God in Christ Jesus.
\f2\b0 \
This is the believer's identification. This is who we are. This is what the Father has done in His Beloved Son.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A QUESTION FOR YOU\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Where would you have us go next, brother? Several rich directions present themselves:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (A) The practical implications of this identification
\f2\b0  \'97 how we 
\f1\i walk
\f2\i0  in this reality (Romans 6, 8, 12; Colossians 3; Galatians 5). The "indicative-to-imperative" of Pauline ethics: because we have this identification, we walk a certain way.\

\f0\b (B) The corporate dimension
\f2\b0  \'97 the believer's identification not only individually with Christ but corporately as the Body of Christ, the Bride of Christ, the Temple of God, the Holy Nation, the Royal Priesthood. This is a separate and rich vein.\

\f0\b (C) The eschatological dimension
\f2\b0  \'97 the consummation of our identification at His return, the resurrection of our bodies, the marriage of the Lamb, the inheritance of the kingdom, the new heavens and new earth.\

\f0\b (D) Any other thread you wish to follow.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 We will examine each of the ones you have enumerated, beginning with D: \'85If we be children, we are also heirs, even the heirs of God, and heirs annexed with Christ: if so be that we suffer with him, that we may also be glorified with him. What suffering(s) with Christ (in a practical sense) are endured by modern day believers?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is 
\f0\b Romans 8:17
\f2\b0 , and it is one of the most consequential conditional statements in the entire NT. Paul attaches a real condition to the believer's co-glorification: 
\f0\b "if so be that we suffer with Him."
\f2\b0  We dare not pass over this casually.\
Let me address this carefully per our maxims:\
1. First, examine what the Greek of Romans 8:17 actually establishes (and what it does not).\
2. Survey the whole NT counsel on what "suffering with Christ" means.\
3. Bring this honestly into the present age for the modern believer.\
4. Be unflinching where Scripture is unflinching, and silent where Scripture is silent.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b ROMANS 8:17 \'97 THE FOUNDATIONAL TEXT
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "If we be children, we are also heirs, even the heirs of God, and heirs annexed with Christ: if so be that we suffer with him, that we may also be glorified with him."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Careful examination of the conditional\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u949 \u7988 \u960 \u949 \u961  \u963 \u965 \u956 \u960 \u940 \u963 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "if indeed / since indeed we suffer together."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7988 \u960 \u949 \u961 
\f2\b0  is a strengthened form of 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7984 
\f2\b0  (if). It can be translated 
\f1\i "if indeed"
\f2\i0  or 
\f1\i "inasmuch as"
\f2\i0  \'97 sometimes carrying the sense of 
\f1\i "seeing that"
\f2\i0  (assuming the condition is in fact met). It is 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  a doubtful "if" \'97 it is more like 
\f1\i "if, as is the case"
\f2\i0  or 
\f1\i "given that."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u965 \u956 \u960 \u940 \u963 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 present active indicative \'97 
\f1\i "we are suffering together [with Christ]."
\f2\i0  The present tense indicates 
\f0\b an ongoing reality
\f2\b0 , not a future possibility. Paul presents co-suffering as the present experience of the believer.\

\f0\b \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u948 \u959 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u8182 \u956 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "in order that we may also be glorified together [with Him]."
\f2\i0  Aorist passive subjunctive \'97 the purpose / result clause. 
\f0\b The co-suffering is the path to the co-glorification.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What this verse establishes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1) Suffering with Christ is normative for the believer.
\f2\b0  Paul does not say 
\f1\i "some believers suffer with Him."
\f2\i0  He presents co-suffering as the present experience of those who are joint-heirs. The \uc0\u949 \u7988 \u960 \u949 \u961  does not introduce a possibility \'97 it confirms an actual condition that characterizes the believer's life.\

\f0\b (2) Co-suffering is the path to co-glorification.
\f2\b0  The Father's design is that the path to glory runs through fellowship with the Son's sufferings. 
\f0\b There is no co-glorification without co-suffering.
\f2\b0  This is not punishment for being a child of God; it is the 
\f0\b pattern of the Beloved Son
\f2\b0 , into whose image we are being conformed (Rom 8:29).\

\f0\b (3) This is corporate to all believers, not an elite calling.
\f2\b0  Paul includes himself and his Roman readers \'97 ordinary believers \'97 in the 
\f1\i "we"
\f2\i0  who suffer together with Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b WHAT DOES "SUFFERING WITH CHRIST" MEAN?
\f2\b0 \
Per our maxims, we must let Scripture itself define this \'97 not project our own assumptions. The NT identifies several distinct yet overlapping categories of suffering that constitute the believer's fellowship with Christ's sufferings.\
Let us survey them carefully.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 CATEGORY 1 \'97 SUFFERING FOR RIGHTEOUSNESS' SAKE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is the most explicit form of suffering with Christ: enduring opposition, hostility, slander, persecution, or harm specifically 
\f1\i because of one's union with Him and obedience to His word.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Blessed are they which suffer persecution for righteousness' sake: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven. Blessed shall ye be when men revile you, and persecute you, and say all manner of evil against you for my sake, falsely. Rejoice and be glad, for great is your reward in heaven: for so persecuted they the Prophets which were before you."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  Three distinct experiences are identified:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8000 \u957 \u949 \u953 \u948 \u943 \u963 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 being reviled / reproached (verbal contempt).\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \u974 \u958 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 being persecuted (active hostility, possibly physical).\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7988 \u960 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u960 \u8118 \u957  \u960 \u959 \u957 \u951 \u961 \u8056 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u968 \u949 \u965 \u948 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 having all manner of evil spoken against you falsely (slander, defamation).\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  The qualifier is critical: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7957 \u957 \u949 \u954 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "for My sake."
\f2\i0  Not all suffering qualifies as "suffering with Christ." It must be 
\f0\b for His sake
\f2\b0  \'97 because of fidelity to Him and His word.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  The pattern continues that of the prophets \'97 those who spoke for God and suffered for it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "If the world hate you, ye know that it hated me before you. If ye were of the world, the world would love his own: but because ye are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world, therefore the world hateth you. Remember the word that I said unto you, The servant is not greater than his master. If they have persecuted me, they will persecute you also..."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1) The world's hatred is a settled disposition.
\f2\b0  Jesus presents it as a constant \'97 the world has hated Him, and will hate those who are His.\

\f0\b (2) The reason: \uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7952 \u954  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u965  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u941 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "because you are not of the world."
\f2\i0  The believer's separation from the world is the cause of the world's hostility. Identification with Christ removes us from the world's love.\

\f0\b (3) The principle: \uc0\u927 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u948 \u959 \u8166 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u956 \u949 \u943 \u950 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "The servant is not greater than his master."
\f2\i0  What He endured, His servants will endure. This is a settled pattern of the Christian life, not an aberration.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Yea, and all that will live godly in Christ Jesus, shall suffer persecution."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of decisive importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u959 \u7985  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u949 \u8016 \u963 \u949 \u946 \u8182 \u962  \u950 \u8134 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u948 \u953 \u969 \u967 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "All who desire to live godly in Christ Jesus shall be persecuted."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "all."
\f2\i0  No exception. 
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \u969 \u967 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 future passive \'97 
\f1\i "will be persecuted."
\f2\i0  A settled, prophetic certainty.\
This is a sobering text. Paul, writing to Timothy near the end of his own life, declares it as a universal principle: 
\f0\b godly living in Christ Jesus brings persecution.
\f2\b0  The form may vary; the reality is constant.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 CATEGORY 2 \'97 SUFFERING THE WORLD'S HATRED FOR HIS NAME\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 A related but distinct facet: suffering specifically because one bears the Name of Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "But all these things will they do unto you for my Name's sake, because they have not known him that sent me."
