\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  Bearing the Name itself can be a cause of suffering. The world's quarrel is ultimately not with the believer personally but 
\f0\b with the Name and the One whose Name it is
\f2\b0  (because they do not know the Father \'97 John 15:21).\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  The apostles' response to this suffering is 
\f0\b rejoicing
\f2\b0  \'97 counted worthy to bear shame for the Name. This is not a stoic endurance but a joyful identification: 
\f1\i "if this is what comes from being identified with Him, blessed are we."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b (3) 1 Peter 4 carefully distinguishes the suffering that pleases God
\f2\b0  (suffering as a Christian, for His Name) 
\f0\b from suffering that does not
\f2\b0  (suffering as a murderer, thief, evildoer, busybody \'97 v. 15). Not all suffering counts as fellowship with Christ; only suffering that arises from identification with Him and His ways.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
