\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  Paul speaks of bearing in his body 
\f0\b the afflictions of Christ for the Body's sake
\f2\b0 . He does not mean the atoning sufferings of Christ are incomplete; he means that 
\f0\b Christ's sufferings, which continue in His Body, are filled up in the apostle's flesh for the Body's benefit.
\f2\b0  The Body of Christ continues to suffer in this age \'97 and faithful ministers bear suffering on behalf of their brethren.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  Paul's sufferings include 
\f0\b the daily burden of care for the churches
\f2\b0  \'97 the emotional, pastoral, intercessory weight of bearing his brethren's burdens. He weeps with them, sympathizes with them, intercedes for them. 
\f0\b When others stumble, he burns; when others are weak, he is weak with them.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
