\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Luke 9:23:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "And he said to them all, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross daily, and follow me."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  Three commands: 
\f0\b deny self, take up the cross, follow.
\f2\b0  Each one a suffering.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b Luke adds \uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u8125  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "daily."
\f2\i0  The cross-bearing is not a one-time act but a daily reality. Each day brings its own self-denial, its own cross.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The "cross" was a Roman instrument of execution.
\f2\b0  When Jesus said "take up your cross," His hearers heard 
\f1\i "go to the place of dying."
\f2\i0  The cross-bearer was a condemned man walking to his execution. Jesus calls every disciple to this posture: 
\f0\b to live as one already given over to death, that he might live unto the Lord.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The paradox:
\f2\b0  saving one's life loses it; losing one's life for Christ's sake finds it. The believer must die to find life. This is a daily reality, not merely an eschatological one.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 CATEGORY 7 \'97 SUFFERING DOWNWARD MOBILITY FOR HIS SAKE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The willing surrender of worldly status, position, possessions, or recognition for the sake of identification with Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Hebrews 11:24-26:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "By faith Moses when he was come to age, refused to be called the son of Pharaoh's daughter, And chose rather to suffer adversity with the people of God, than to enjoy the pleasures of sins for a season, Esteeming the rebuke of Christ greater riches than the treasures of Egypt: for he had respect unto the recompense of the reward."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Philippians 3:7-8:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "But the things that were vantage unto me, the same I counted loss for Christ's sake. Yea, doubtless I think all things but loss for the excellent knowledge sake of Christ Jesus my Lord, for whom I have counted all things loss, and do judge them to be dung, that I might win Christ,"
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1) Moses gave up royalty and the treasures of Egypt
\f2\b0  \'97 choosing rather to 
\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u965 \u947 \u954 \u945 \u954 \u959 \u965 \u967 \u949 \u8150 \u963 \u952 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8183  \u955 \u945 \u8183  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to suffer affliction together with the people of God."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b (2) He esteemed \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u8000 \u957 \u949 \u953 \u948 \u953 \u963 \u956 \u8056 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \'97 "the reproach of Christ"
\f2\b0  as greater riches than the treasures of Egypt. This is remarkable \'97 Moses, in advance of the incarnation, bore "the reproach of Christ" by his identification with God's people. 
\f0\b The reproach of identification with Christ is a treasure.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (3) Paul echoes this:
\f2\b0  All his Jewish pedigree, his pharisaical standing, his learning, his accomplishments \'97 
\f0\b all counted as loss, even as \uc0\u963 \u954 \u973 \u946 \u945 \u955 \u945  (refuse, dung)
\f2\b0  \'97 for the surpassing worth of knowing Christ.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  This is a real suffering \'97 the loss of what the world esteems, willingly endured for the sake of Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 CATEGORY 8 \'97 SUFFERING THE CHASTENING OF THE FATHER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 A facet often misunderstood \'97 the Father's loving discipline of His children.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Hebrews 12:5-11, selections:\
1599 Geneva (selections):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "...My son, despise not the chastening of the Lord, neither faint when thou art rebuked of him. For whom the Lord loveth, he chasteneth: and he scourgeth every son that he receiveth... If ye endure chastening, God offereth himself unto you as unto sons: for what son is it whom the father chasteneth not? If therefore ye be without correction, whereof all are partakers, then are ye bastards, and not sons... Now no chastising for the present seemeth to be joyous, but, grievous: but afterward, it bringeth the quiet fruit of righteousness, unto them which are thereby exercised."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  The Father chastens those He loves. Chastening is 
\f0\b evidence of sonship
\f2\b0 , not exclusion from it.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  This chastening is sometimes experienced through circumstances \'97 adversity, loss, trial \'97 which the Father uses to correct, train, and conform us to His Son's image.\

\f0\b (3) Not all such suffering is for specific sin
\f2\b0  \'97 sometimes it is for general training in holiness. Even the Son was perfected through what He suffered (Heb 5:8). The believer's path is the same pattern.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b BRINGING THIS HONESTLY INTO THE MODERN BELIEVER'S LIFE
\f2\b0 \
Now we must ask honestly: 
\f0\b how does this present itself in the life of a modern believer in 2024-2025 in (presumably) the Western world?
\f2\b0 \
Per our maxims, we must not pretend the modern Western believer faces what believers in many places still face (imprisonment, beating, execution for their faith). But we also must not dismiss the real sufferings he or she does endure as somehow not counting. Let me address this carefully.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1. Open Persecution in Much of the World \'97 Real and Present\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We must first acknowledge: 
\f0\b in many parts of the world today, believers face Category 1 persecution in the most explicit form.
\f2\b0  In North Korea, in parts of China, in Saudi Arabia, in Iran, in Afghanistan, in Nigeria, in Eritrea, in Pakistan, in India, in numerous other places \'97 believers today are:\
- 
\f0\b Imprisoned
\f2\b0  for their faith.\
- 
\f0\b Tortured
\f2\b0  for their faith.\
- 
\f0\b Killed
\f2\b0  for their faith.\
- 
\f0\b Separated from families
\f2\b0  for their faith.\
- 
\f0\b Denied employment, education, civil rights
\f2\b0  for their faith.\
- 
\f0\b Watching their children sold or trafficked
\f2\b0  for their faith.\
- 
\f0\b Driven from their homes and villages
\f2\b0  for their faith.\
The believer's suffering with Christ has 
\f0\b not lessened
\f2\b0  in our day; in many ways, statistics suggest that more believers are being killed for their faith in this present age than in any previous generation. 
\f0\b The Western reader must remember the global body of Christ.
\f2\b0  We are in fellowship with these brethren \'97 
\f0\b "remember those in bonds as bound with them"
\f2\b0  (Heb 13:3).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 2. Increasing Cultural Hostility in the Western World\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The modern Western believer faces what is perhaps best described as 
\f0\b soft persecution
\f2\b0  \'97 but persecution nonetheless. Specifically:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Reviling and slander (Matt 5:11):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - Being mocked or ridiculed in media, education, or public discourse for biblical convictions.\
- Being labeled with stigmatizing words (
\f1\i "bigot," "hateful," "intolerant," "phobic"
\f2\i0 ) for holding to plain biblical teaching on creation, marriage, gender, sexual morality, the exclusivity of Christ, the authority of Scripture.\
- Having one's character, motives, or intelligence impugned because of one's faith.\
This is real 
\f0\b \uc0\u8000 \u957 \u949 \u953 \u948 \u953 \u963 \u956 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i reproach
\f2\i0  \'97 for the Name. Not on the scale of imprisonment, but real nonetheless, and increasing in intensity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Loss of social, professional, or educational standing:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - Believers who openly affirm biblical convictions in workplaces, universities, professional bodies, government, military, or media increasingly face:\
- Discrimination in hiring and promotion.\
- Pressure to participate in or affirm what conscience forbids.\
- Loss of jobs, contracts, licenses, or platforms for refusing.\
- Exclusion from professional associations.\
- Censorship on social media and digital platforms.\
This is real 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u943 \u948 \u969 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i suffering loss
\f2\i0  \'97 and corresponds to what Moses chose: identification with God's people over the treasures and standing of Egypt (Heb 11:24-26).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Legal and civic pressures:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - In some Western jurisdictions, believers face legal action for biblical speech regarded as "hate speech."\
- Christian schools, universities, charities, and businesses face mounting legal restrictions for adhering to biblical convictions.\
- Parents face challenges over the upbringing of their children in faith.\
- Conscience protections are eroding.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Family rupture:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Jesus warned that the Gospel would divide families (Matt 10:34-37). Many modern believers \'97 particularly converts from unbelieving, hostile religious, or ideological backgrounds \'97 experience:\
- Estrangement from parents, siblings, or extended family.\
- Loss of marriage relationships when an unbelieving spouse rejects the believer's conversion.\
- Loss of children who reject the faith and reject the parent.\
- Loss of friendships of long standing.\
This is a deep, ongoing suffering \'97 and is borne 
\f0\b for His sake
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 3. The Internal Sufferings of the Faithful Walk (Category 3 \'97 Daily Dying)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The modern believer who walks faithfully experiences daily what Paul called 
\f1\i "always bearing about in the body the dying of the Lord Jesus"
\f2\i0  (2 Cor 4:10). This includes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Mortification of the flesh:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The daily putting to death of sinful desires, habits, thought-patterns (Col 3:5; Rom 8:13).\
- Saying no to legitimate pleasures when they would compromise fidelity to Christ.\
- Choosing the harder right over the easier wrong.\
This is 
\f0\b a real suffering
\f2\b0  \'97 the flesh resists, the world tempts, and yielding to the Spirit costs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The conflict within (Rom 7, Gal 5):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The ongoing tension between the indwelling Spirit and the remaining flesh.\
- The grief of besetting sins, repeated failures, and slow growth.\
- The earnest desire for holiness, paired with painful awareness of imperfection.\
This conflict itself is a form of suffering \'97 the very fact that we groan over our remaining sinfulness is part of our co-suffering with Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The cost of standing firm in truth:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - Refusing to compromise on the Father's truth when it would be socially easier to soften it.\
- Speaking the truth in love when silence would be more comfortable.\
- Disciplining children, congregations, or oneself when permissiveness would be easier.\
- Confronting sin in a brother (Matt 18) when avoidance would be easier.\
Each of these is a small daily cross.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 4. The Sufferings of the Fallen Creation (Category 4)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Every believer endures the sufferings common to all in the fallen creation \'97 but bears them 
\f0\b with hope
\f2\b0 :\
- 
\f0\b Bodily afflictions:
\f2\b0  illness, injury, disability, the weakness of aging, chronic conditions, mental suffering, depression, anxiety.\
- 
\f0\b The grief of bereavement:
\f2\b0  the death of loved ones, the experience of separation and loss.\
- 
\f0\b Economic hardship:
\f2\b0  poverty, job loss, financial pressure, debt.\
- 
\f0\b Relational pain:
\f2\b0  broken relationships, betrayal, loneliness, marital difficulty, the heartbreak of wayward children.\
- 
\f0\b Natural disasters, accidents, the violence of others
\f2\b0  \'97 all the consequences of a creation under the curse.\
The believer is 
\f0\b not exempted
\f2\b0  from any of these. What is changed is the 
\f0\b relation
\f2\b0  to them: the believer suffers 
\f0\b with hope
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b as a child of the Father
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b in fellowship with the Son who also suffered in a fallen world
\f2\b0 .\
These are not "punishments." They are the conditions of life in this age \'97 and the Father uses them all for the conformity of His children to the image of His Son (Rom 8:28-29).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 5. The Burden of Brotherly Love (Category 5)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The faithful believer who genuinely loves the Body of Christ will inevitably suffer:\
- 
\f0\b For wayward brethren
\f2\b0  \'97 burdened in prayer, grieved over their drift.\
- 
\f0\b With suffering brethren
\f2\b0  \'97 entering into their pain, weeping with those who weep (Rom 12:15).\
- 
\f0\b In intercession
\f2\b0  \'97 the long, often hidden labor of prayer for the saints.\
- 
\f0\b In service
\f2\b0  \'97 pouring out time, resources, energy for the building up of the Body.\
- 
\f0\b Through false teachers and divisions
\f2\b0  \'97 the heartbreak of watching the Body of Christ fractured by those who would mislead or divide.\
- 
\f0\b In the work of the Gospel
\f2\b0  \'97 the burden of evangelism, the weight of rejection by those one labors to win.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 6. The Daily Cross-Bearing of Discipleship (Category 6)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Every believer is called to 
\f0\b daily
\f2\b0  self-denial (Luke 9:23). This includes:\
- 
\f0\b Denying self-will
\f2\b0  in submission to the Father's will.\
- 
\f0\b Denying the desire for ease
\f2\b0  in choosing the path of obedience.\
- 
\f0\b Denying the desire for vindication
\f2\b0  in entrusting wrongs to the Father.\
- 
\f0\b Denying the desire for approval
\f2\b0  in choosing fidelity to Christ over the praise of men.\
- 
\f0\b Denying lawful pleasures
\f2\b0  when they would crowd out devotion.\
The cross is taken up 
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u8125  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i daily
\f2\i0 . There is no Christian life without it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b WHAT IS NOT "SUFFERING WITH CHRIST"
\f2\b0 \
Per our maxims, we should also note honestly what does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  qualify as suffering with Christ \'97 lest the modern believer claim credit where Scripture gives none.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Peter's distinction (1 Peter 4:15-16):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 1599 Geneva:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "But if any man suffer as a Christian, let him not be ashamed... But let none of you suffer as a murderer, or as a thief, or an evil doer, or as a busybody in other men's matters."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b Suffering brought on by one's own foolishness, sin, lawlessness, or meddling does not qualify.
\f2\b0  A believer who suffers consequences for his own actions is not thereby "suffering with Christ" \'97 he is suffering for his own folly.\
This includes:\
- Suffering caused by our own sin or sinful patterns.\
- Suffering caused by our own pride, contentiousness, or unkindness \'97 which we may dress up as "persecution for righteousness' sake" when in fact it is reaction to our own carnality.\
- Suffering caused by our own poor judgment, indolence, or irresponsibility.\
- Self-imposed suffering (asceticism not commanded by God) \'97 Paul rebukes this in Col 2:20-23.\
The modern believer must be honest in self-examination: 
\f0\b is this truly persecution for the Name and the truth, or am I merely facing the consequences of my own actions or attitudes?
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b THE GIFTS THAT ACCOMPANY THE SUFFERING
\f2\b0 \
Scripture is careful to surround the doctrine of co-suffering with 
\f0\b comfort, promise, and assurance
\f2\b0  \'97 not to soften the reality but to sustain the believer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Romans 8:18:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "For I count that the afflictions of this present time are not worthy of the glory, which shall be showed unto us."
\f2\i0 \
The sufferings of this present age are 
\f0\b not worthy of comparison
\f2\b0  with the coming glory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2 Corinthians 4:17:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "For our light affliction which is but for a moment, causeth unto us a far most excellent and an eternal weight of glory:"
\f2\i0 \
The present afflictions are working out 
\f0\b a far more exceeding and eternal weight of glory.
\f2\b0  The pain is producing the glory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Philippians 1:29:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "For unto you it is given for Christ, that not only ye should believe in him, but also suffer for his sake,"
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Both faith in Christ AND suffering for Him are gifts
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "have been graciously given"
\f2\i0  \'97 from the same hand of grace. The suffering is a divine gift, not a divine punishment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1 Peter 4:12-13:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "Dearly beloved, think it not strange concerning the fiery trial, which is among you to prove you, as though some strange thing were come unto you: But rejoice, inasmuch as ye are partakers of Christ's sufferings, that when his glory shall appear, ye may be glad and rejoice."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Do not think it strange.
\f2\b0  The fiery trial is normative, not abnormal. 
\f0\b Rejoice
\f2\b0  \'97 for you are sharing in His sufferings, and you will share in His glory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
