\cf0 # 
\f0\b THE GOVERNING PATTERN: INDICATIVE \uc0\u8594  RECKON \u8594  ACT
\f2\b0 \
Romans 6 establishes the fundamental Christian operation:\
1. 
\f0\b Know what God has done
\f2\b0  (the indicative \'97 vv. 1-10).\
2. 
\f0\b Reckon it true of yourself
\f2\b0  (v. 11).\
3. 
\f0\b Act on the reckoning
\f2\b0  (vv. 12-13).\
This is the precise reverse of the world's pattern, which is:\
1. 
\f1\i Try to act righteously.
\f2\i0 \
2. 
\f1\i Hope to become righteous through your acts.
\f2\i0 \
3. 
\f1\i Believe in your status only after performance.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Gospel pattern is the opposite:
\f2\b0 \
1. 
\f1\i You ARE righteous in Christ (indicative).
\f2\i0 \
2. 
\f1\i Reckon it true (faith).
\f2\i0 \
3. 
\f1\i Act consistently with what is true (obedience).
\f2\i0 \
The Christian does not act in order to become; he acts because he has become.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b CROSS-WITNESSES \'97 THE PATTERN ELSEWHERE
\f2\b0 \
This indicative-to-imperative pattern is not unique to Romans 6 \'97 it is the fundamental pattern of all NT ethics. Let us confirm by examining the most explicit parallels.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 EPHESIANS \'97 THE INDICATIVE OF CHAPTERS 1-3, THE IMPERATIVE OF 4-6\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The entire epistle to the Ephesians displays this pattern on a grand scale.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Chapters 1-3 are pure indicative:
\f2\b0 \
- Chosen in Him before the foundation of the world (1:4).\
- Predestined to adoption (1:5).\
- Accepted in the Beloved (1:6).\
- Redeemed through His blood (1:7).\
- Sealed with the Holy Spirit (1:13).\
- Made alive together with Christ (2:5).\
- Raised up together (2:6).\
- Seated together in the heavenly places in Christ Jesus (2:6).\
- Fellow-citizens with the saints (2:19).\
- Members of God's household (2:19).\
- Built together for a habitation of God (2:22).\
- Filled with the fullness of God (3:19).\

\f0\b Chapters 4-6 are pure imperative \'97 and they begin with the pivot word.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Ephesians 4:1:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "I therefore, being prisoner in the Lord, pray you that ye walk worthy of the vocation whereunto ye are called,"
\f2\i0 \
The word 
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u8022 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "therefore"
\f2\i0  \'97 is the pivot. Three chapters of indicative produce one 
\f1\i "therefore"
\f2\i0  that launches three chapters of imperative.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The imperative of Ephesians 4-6 is grounded entirely in the indicative of Ephesians 1-3.
\f2\b0  Walk worthy of the calling \'97 
\f1\i because of all that Christ has already accomplished in you.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 COLOSSIANS 3 \'97 THE EXPLICIT CONNECTION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Colossians 3:1-5:\
1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "If ye then be risen with Christ, seek those things which are above, where Christ sitteth at the right hand of God. Set your affections on things which are above, and not on things which are on the earth. For ye are dead, and your life is hid with Christ in God. When Christ which is our life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with him in glory. Mortify therefore your members which are on the earth..."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The pattern is perfectly visible:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b Indicative (v. 1):
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "If you have been raised with Christ..."
\f2\i0  \'97 you have been.\
- 
\f0\b Indicative (v. 3):
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "For you died, and your life is hidden with Christ in God."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Indicative (v. 4):
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "You shall appear with Him in glory."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Imperative (v. 1):
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "Seek those things which are above."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Imperative (v. 2):
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "Set your affection on things above."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Imperative (v. 5):
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "Mortify therefore your members which are on the earth..."
\f2\i0 \
The word 
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u8022 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "therefore"
\f2\i0  \'97 appears again as the pivot in v. 5. 
\f0\b Because you have died (indicative), therefore mortify your members (imperative).
\f2\b0 \
This is the same Romans 6 pattern, restated.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 GALATIANS 5:24-25 \'97 A SUCCINCT STATEMENT\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "For they that are Christ's, have crucified the flesh, with the affections and the lusts. If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 v. 24 \'97 Indicative:
\f2\b0  Those who belong to Christ 
\f0\b have crucified
\f2\b0  the flesh. The verb is aorist \'97 completed past action.\

\f0\b v. 25 \'97 Imperative based on the indicative:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit."
\f2\i0  Since we live by the Spirit (an established reality), let us walk by the Spirit (the corresponding action).\
The same pattern in compressed form.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 EPHESIANS 4:22-24 \'97 PUTTING OFF AND PUTTING ON\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "That is, that ye cast off, concerning the conversation in time past, that old man, which is corrupt through the deceivable lusts, And be renewed in the spirit of your mind, And put on the new man, which after God is created unto righteousness, and true holiness."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The believer is to 
\f0\b put off
\f2\b0  the old man and 
\f0\b put on
\f2\b0  the new man. But notice: 
\f0\b the new man has already been created \'97 \uc0\u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u964 \u945  \'97 perfect tense.
\f2\b0  The new man is not something the believer creates by his obedience; the new man has been created by God in Christ. The believer 
\f0\b puts on
\f2\b0  what already exists in him through new creation.\
This is the same indicative-imperative pattern: 
\f0\b the new man exists (indicative); put him on (imperative).
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b THE PRACTICAL IMPLICATIONS FOR THE MODERN BELIEVER
\f2\b0 \
Now we must bring this home to daily life. How does the Romans 6 pattern reshape the practical walk of the modern believer?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1. The Reckoning Is the Daily Foundation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The believer's daily life begins with 
\f0\b the reckoning of v. 11.
\f2\b0  This is not a one-time event at conversion; it is a moment-by-moment posture of mind.\
When the believer wakes in the morning, he must reckon:\
- 
\f1\i "I am dead to sin. I am alive to God in Christ Jesus."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "I have been crucified with Christ; the life I now live in the flesh, I live by faith of the Son of God."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "My life is hidden with Christ in God."
\f2\i0 \
This reckoning is 
\f0\b faith applied to identity
\f2\b0  \'97 and it is the basis on which the day's obedience proceeds.\
When temptation comes during the day, the believer's first response is not 
\f1\i "I must resist this"
\f2\i0  but 
\f1\i "I am dead to this. Sin no longer has dominion over me. I am alive to God in Christ Jesus. I refuse the throne to sin."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The believer fights from victory, not for victory.
\f2\b0  The victory has been won at the cross. The fight is to walk in what has been won.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 2. The Body Is to Be Presented, Not Indulged\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The body is mortal and still bears the desires that can be exploited by sin. 
\f0\b But the body is not to be allowed to dictate.
\f2\b0  The believer presents his body to God as a living sacrifice (Rom 12:1).\
This means practically:\
- 
\f0\b The eyes:
\f2\b0  what we look at \'97 are they weapons of righteousness or unrighteousness?\
- 
\f0\b The ears:
\f2\b0  what we listen to \'97 does it build us up or pull us toward sin?\
- 
\f0\b The tongue:
\f2\b0  what we speak \'97 does it bless or curse, edify or tear down?\
- 
\f0\b The hands:
\f2\b0  what we do \'97 are they instruments of service to God or to self/sin?\
- 
\f0\b The feet:
\f2\b0  where we go \'97 are they leading us toward righteousness or temptation?\
- 
\f0\b The mind:
\f2\b0  what we dwell on \'97 are our thoughts being taken captive to obey Christ (2 Cor 10:5)?\
- 
\f0\b The heart's affections:
\f2\b0  what we love \'97 are they set on things above (Col 3:1-2)?\
The believer presents each member of his body, daily and moment by moment, to God as a weapon of righteousness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 3. Sin's Authority Is Refused, Not Negotiated With\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The believer does not negotiate with sin. He does not say, 
\f1\i "Maybe a little bit is okay."
\f2\i0  He refuses sin's authority entirely.\
When sin makes its claim \'97 
\f1\i "You always do this; it's who you are; you might as well give in"
\f2\i0  \'97 the believer responds:\
- 
\f1\i "You are speaking to a dead man. I died to you at the cross."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "My identity is not in you. I am in Christ Jesus."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "I refuse you the throne. Christ is Lord."
\f2\i0 \
The fight is to 
\f0\b agree with reality
\f2\b0  \'97 to refuse the lie that we are still slaves and to stand in the freedom Christ has purchased.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 4. The Walk Is in Newness of Life\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The believer's walk is 
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962  \u950 \u969 \u8134 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i newness of life
\f2\i0  (Rom 6:4). This is not an effort to keep old rules; it is a new mode of being.\
Practically, this means:\
- A new orientation: toward the Father, in the Son, by the Spirit.\
- New affections: loving what the Father loves, hating what He hates.\
- New motivations: not for self-preservation or self-glory, but for the glory of the Father in the Son.\
- New patterns: turning from the courses of the world to the path of Christ.\
- New companions (where possible): seeking fellowship with the saints rather than communion with the world.\
- New speech, new habits, new disciplines: increasingly conforming to the pattern of Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The new walk flows from the new identity.
\f2\b0  It is not a list of behaviors to perform; it is a life to live out of who we are in Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 5. Failure Is Met with Reckoning, Not Despair\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 When the believer fails \'97 when sin gains a momentary victory, when the old patterns reassert themselves \'97 the response is 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  to abandon the indicative.\
The response is to 
\f0\b return to the reckoning.
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f1\i "I have failed, but I have not become what I once was."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "My identity is in Christ, not in this failure."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "I confess and turn, knowing that the blood of Christ cleanses me from all sin (1 John 1:7-9)."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "I reckon myself again dead to sin and alive to God in Christ Jesus."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f1\i "I present myself again to God."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The reckoning is repeated, not abandoned.
\f2\b0  The believer does not lose his identity through failure; he reaffirms his identity in confession and continues to walk.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 6. The Spirit Enables What the Reckoning Affirms\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The reckoning is not a self-help technique. 
\f0\b The reckoning is faith in the work of the Father, accomplished in the Son, and applied by the Spirit.
\f2\b0 \
The indwelling Spirit (whom we examined in Parts E and F) is the agent who 
\f0\b makes the reckoning real in experience.
\f2\b0  The Spirit witnesses with our spirit that we are children of God (Rom 8:16). The Spirit produces the fruit of conformity to Christ (Gal 5:22-23). The Spirit puts to death the deeds of the body (Rom 8:13).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The believer reckons; the Spirit empowers.
\f2\b0  These are not two competing realities but one \'97 the Father's work in us, mediated by the Son, applied by the Spirit, received by our faithful reckoning.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 7. The Pattern Is Repeated in Every Sphere\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Romans 6 pattern (indicative \uc0\u8594  reckon \u8594  act) applies to every sphere of the Christian life:\

