\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Single Practical Theology\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 What emerges from all three passages is 
\f0\b one coherent doctrine of practical sanctification:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The believer who has died with Christ, been raised with Him, is seated with Him at the Father's right hand, and is indwelt by the Spirit \'97 this believer is to walk in newness of life by:
\f2\b0 \
1. 
\f0\b Presenting his body as a living sacrifice
\f2\b0  (Rom 12:1) / 
\f0\b mortifying his earthly members
\f2\b0  (Col 3:5) \'97 the comprehensive yielding of the physical body to God.\
2. 
\f0\b Being renewed in the mind
\f2\b0  (Rom 12:2; Col 3:10) \'97 the ongoing transformation of the inner orientation by the Word and the Spirit.\
3. 
\f0\b Walking by the Spirit
\f2\b0  (Gal 5:16) \'97 depending moment by moment on the Spirit's leading and empowering.\
4. 
\f0\b Putting off the works of the old man
\f2\b0  (Col 3:5-9; Gal 5:19-21) \'97 actively refusing the patterns of the flesh.\
5. 
\f0\b Putting on the new man
\f2\b0  (Col 3:10-14) \'97 actively cultivating the patterns of Christ's character.\
6. 
\f0\b Walking in love
\f2\b0  (Rom 12:9-21; Gal 5:13-14; Col 3:14) \'97 the unifying principle of all Christian practice.\
7. 
\f0\b Doing all in the Name of the Lord Jesus, with thanksgiving to the Father
\f2\b0  (Col 3:17) \'97 the comprehensive governing principle.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Practical Modern Application\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 For the modern believer, this means:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 In the morning:
\f2\b0  Reckon yourself dead to sin and alive to God. Present your body to the Father as a living sacrifice. Set your mind on things above. Open the Word and feed the renewing process.\

\f0\b Throughout the day:
\f2\b0  Walk by the Spirit. Yield to His leading. Put off the works of the flesh as they arise. Put on the characteristics of Christ. Do every word and deed in the Name of the Lord Jesus, with thanksgiving.\

\f0\b In relationships:
\f2\b0  Love without dissimulation. Bless those who persecute. Forgive as Christ has forgiven. Honor your spouse, parents, children, employer, employees, brethren. Be at peace with all men so far as it depends on you. Overcome evil with good.\

\f0\b In the mind:
\f2\b0  Resist the world's mold. Embrace the Spirit's transformation. Think on what is true, honorable, just, pure, lovely, of good report. Take every thought captive to obey Christ. Renew the mind through Scripture, prayer, and fellowship.\

\f0\b In moments of failure:
\f2\b0  Return immediately to the reckoning. Confess. Trust the cleansing blood. Receive forgiveness. Get up and walk again. Do not despair; do not abandon the walk; do not let one failure define the day.\

\f0\b In suffering:
\f2\b0  Recognize the Father's purpose \'97 conformity to the Son. Trust that all things work together for good. Hold fast the unshakable hope. Look beyond present sufferings to the coming glory.\

\f0\b In all things:
\f2\b0  Live as one who belongs to the Father, walks in the Son, is indwelt by the Spirit, and is destined for glory. 
\f0\b You are not who you were. You are in Christ. Walk worthy.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b A CLOSING OBSERVATION
\f2\b0 \
Brother, what we have surveyed in these three passages is 
\f0\b the genius of the New Testament's ethic.
\f2\b0  It is not a system of rules to be followed; it is a life to be lived out of who we already are. It is not the achievement of an unreal status; it is the working out of what is positionally true.\
The modern believer who walks in this reality is:\
- 
\f0\b Free
\f2\b0  \'97 from law as a means of justification, from the flesh as a master, from the world as a mold.\
- 
\f0\b Empowered
\f2\b0  \'97 by the indwelling Spirit who produces what the believer cannot manufacture.\
- 
\f0\b Oriented
\f2\b0  \'97 toward the things above, where Christ is seated.\
- 
\f0\b Renewed
\f2\b0  \'97 in the mind, progressively conformed to the Son's image.\
- 
\f0\b Engaged
\f2\b0  \'97 in active putting off and putting on, by the Spirit's power.\
- 
\f0\b In love
\f2\b0  \'97 the unifying principle of all Christian practice.\
- 
\f0\b In community
\f2\b0  \'97 for the new humanity transcends every former division.\
- 
\f0\b In every sphere
\f2\b0  \'97 for nothing in the believer's life is exempt from the Lordship of Christ.\
This is what the Father's eternal purpose looks like in daily practice. This is what it means to be 
\f0\b a child of the Father, in the Beloved Son, by the indwelling Spirit, walking by faith until He appears.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b A QUESTION FOR YOU
\f2\b0 \
Where would you have us go next?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (A)
\f2\b0  Move now to the 
\f0\b corporate dimension
\f2\b0  \'97 the Body of Christ, the Bride of Christ, the Temple of God, the Holy Nation, the Royal Priesthood?\

\f0\b (B)
\f2\b0  Examine the 
\f0\b eschatological consummation
\f2\b0  \'97 the resurrection of the body, the marriage of the Lamb, the new heavens and new earth, the inheritance of the kingdom?\

\f0\b (C)
\f2\b0  A specific aspect of the practical walk you wish to examine more carefully \'97 perhaps prayer, the use of Scripture, the believer's response to specific kinds of trials, or the spiritual disciplines?\

\f0\b (D)
\f2\b0  Another direction of your choosing?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Yes, let\'92s do a thorough (exhaustive) examination of all relevant aspects of C above\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

